WEBVTT

1
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:17,350
[narrator] <i>Long, long ago,</i>
<i>a great calamity emerged</i>

2
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:19,227
<i>from the depths of the Ashen Sea.</i>

3
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:22,605
<i>Its form was that of a great beast</i>
<i>that destroyed all in its path,</i>

4
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:24,816
<i>and Nergal was its name.</i>

5
00:00:24,899 --> 00:00:28,194
<i>Through the ages, many warriors</i>
<i>challenged the malevolent force</i>

6
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:31,990
<i>known as the King of Ash,</i>
<i>but all were defeated.</i>

7
00:00:33,992 --> 00:00:36,911
<i>People had given up</i>
<i>on fighting the threat so long ago,</i>

8
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:39,497
<i>the idea of resisting</i>
<i>seemed a distant memory.</i>

9
00:00:40,331 --> 00:00:44,044
<i>But then a new warrior</i>
<i>was about to be born.</i>

10
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:53,845
[electrical buzzing]

11
00:00:55,263 --> 00:00:56,973
[theatrical music playing]

12
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:24,542
[gasps]

13
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:28,296
[Zirco sobbing] Sapphire! Oh, Sapphire!

14
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:30,507
Oh, please, please!

15
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:33,968
Sapphire, please. Sapphire!

16
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:35,887
[Sapphire groans]

17
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,681
[Zirco] Are you all right?

18
00:01:41,059 --> 00:01:42,143
Sapphire, wait.

19
00:01:42,727 --> 00:01:44,395
Your arm.

20
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:48,066
-[Sapphire] I'm fine…
-Ooh, ooh.

21
00:01:48,691 --> 00:01:49,526
…Zirco.

22
00:01:52,111 --> 00:01:52,946
[both gasp]

23
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:56,116
[Sapphire] What happened?

24
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:00,370
It's all destroyed. There's nothing left.

25
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:05,708
[Sapphire groaning softly]

26
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:10,004
[mumbled voice in a distance]

27
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:12,257
Ah. Mother, is that you?

28
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:16,177
-[mumbled voice in a distance continues]
-[Sapphire whimpers]

29
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:18,721
[Sapphire] Mother! I'll get you out!

30
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:23,143
[Zirco] Don't hurt yourself more.

31
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:26,396
It must be blocked by the rubble.

32
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:28,398
Mother, I'm coming!

33
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:30,859
I'm gonna get you out of there! Hold on!

34
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:34,320
[Queen] Sapphire, it's no use.

35
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:35,530
What?

36
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:39,284
No, Mother! What do you mean?
I can defeat the Nergal!

37
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,287
<i>I'm more powerful than that thing!</i>

38
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:45,623
I'll put an end to that atrocity
once and for all!

39
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:49,752
Damn it! I'll open the door!
Open up! I'll save you all!

40
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:52,380
I'll save you and Father
and everyone in the kingdom!

41
00:02:52,463 --> 00:02:56,467
I'm going to protect everyone,
every last person! So, open up!

42
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,052
[sobbing] Come on! Mother!

43
00:02:58,136 --> 00:03:01,514
{\an8}Open the door, Mother! Help me! Open it!

44
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:04,434
{\an8}Trying to fight against this world
is meaningless.

45
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:06,728
{\an8}Why can't you understand that?

46
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:12,775
You're going to have to face the truth,
Sapphire. We've been defeated.

47
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:18,364
[Sapphire] But, Mother, why would…

48
00:03:18,448 --> 00:03:20,617
No, not yet. I'll stay and fight.

49
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:23,536
I'll destroy that Nergal,
whatever it takes!

50
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:25,079
{\an8}[Queen] Sapphire,

51
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:28,041
{\an8}there's nothing you can do to stop it.

52
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:30,877
{\an8}It's over. Accept it.

53
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:37,216
{\an8}The only way that we can survive
is to flee from those stronger than them.

54
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:40,845
{\an8}This whole world can perish and rot,

55
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:44,015
-but my final wish… [muffled speaking]
-[rumbling]

56
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:46,351
No, I…

57
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:48,937
[sobbing] Mother, no! Please!

58
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:51,648
-Open the door! You can't!
-I'm sorry,

59
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:54,067
-Mother, you can't!
-but I've gotta get out of here.

60
00:03:54,150 --> 00:03:56,694
-[Sapphire] Stop it! Let go!
-[Zirco straining]

61
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:59,239
[Sapphire] Let go of me!

62
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:04,535
[rumbling]

63
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:20,593
[passengers whimpering,
indistinct talking]

64
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,307
[groans softly]

65
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:34,941
[Sapphire] The Nergal.

66
00:04:39,529 --> 00:04:40,697
[cawing]

67
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:55,295
[rumbling in distance]

68
00:04:55,878 --> 00:04:57,422
[Sapphire groaning]

69
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:00,800
Oh?

70
00:05:00,883 --> 00:05:02,176
[Zirco] Sapphire!

71
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:17,233
[Zirco chuckling]

72
00:05:18,234 --> 00:05:22,113
Ah! I'm soaked to the bone.
All righty then.

73
00:05:23,031 --> 00:05:24,574
[groans softly]

74
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:28,369
What are you doing over there, Zirco?

75
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:30,913
[Zirco] I'm making you
a little something special.

76
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:32,332
Special?

77
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:35,168
Something that ought to help
liven up your spirits.

78
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:37,253
You know I'm not in the mood
to do anything.

79
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:41,632
Besides, Mother always told me
to avoid doing anything unnecessary.

80
00:05:42,675 --> 00:05:45,303
[Zirco] Well, I'll have to offer
the Queen my contrition,

81
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:48,306
because this is your new weapon, Sapphire.

82
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:51,684
A weapon suited
to help us survive out here.

83
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:56,397
It will allow you to hold things,
to carry things, and even to hug people.

84
00:05:57,315 --> 00:05:58,858
If we hope to make it in this world,

85
00:05:58,941 --> 00:06:01,652
we're going to have to start working
and earning our keep.

86
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:06,574
That's not the same.

87
00:06:10,661 --> 00:06:11,704
[low growl]

88
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:18,961
[gasps] Oh, no.

89
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:22,298
[groaning]

90
00:06:22,381 --> 00:06:23,966
[straining]

91
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:27,428
{\an8}Trying to fight against this world
is meaningless.

92
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:29,222
{\an8}Why can't you understand that?

93
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:35,436
[screams]

94
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:44,612
[Zirco] What's all the ruckus?

95
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:48,533
[screams] Sapphire! Look out!

96
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:52,662
[Sapphire groans]

97
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:56,833
[effort scream]

98
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:01,379
[grunts]

99
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:03,047
Huh?

100
00:07:06,134 --> 00:07:08,553
-Oh, Sapphire!
-[gasps]

101
00:07:08,636 --> 00:07:11,639
Oh, thank goodness you're all right.

102
00:07:11,722 --> 00:07:13,558
-[Sapphire] Zirco.
-[sobbing]

103
00:07:19,063 --> 00:07:20,731
[enchanting music playing]

104
00:07:41,544 --> 00:07:43,463
[electrical buzzing]

105
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:51,512
[choir music playing]

106
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:52,847
Now let us pray.

107
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:56,058
May the Angel of Hope guide us.

108
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,853
[congregation] May the Angel of Hope
guide us.

109
00:08:13,159 --> 00:08:14,577
[indistinct chatter]

110
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:15,995
[woman] Here you go. Thank you.

111
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:17,455
[girl] No, thank you.

112
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:19,916
And I hope you enjoy it.

113
00:08:24,086 --> 00:08:25,213
[man] One loaf, please.

114
00:08:25,296 --> 00:08:26,339
Here you go.

115
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:31,219
I, uh, don't suppose you could make
the loaf a little cheaper today.

116
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:33,137
-Uh--
-It's just, work's been drying up,

117
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:35,056
and I'm barely making it as is.

118
00:08:35,139 --> 00:08:36,349
Uh, well, I…

119
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:39,435
[chuckles]

120
00:08:40,353 --> 00:08:41,312
[sighs]

121
00:08:48,986 --> 00:08:51,072
[moaning weakly]

122
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:54,408
[screams]

123
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:59,747
[eerily] Can you spare some food, please?

124
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:02,208
[groans]

125
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:03,709
Jeez, come on.

126
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:05,461
What am I supposed to do?

127
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:07,797
Um, you all right?

128
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,091
[Sapphire sniffing] Smells so good.

129
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:14,512
Ah! That smell! That smells amazing!

130
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:20,101
{\an8}Uh, well, uh… See, I'm selling them
for 50 gold each. Interested?

131
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:23,729
{\an8}I should have known. I don't have any.

132
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:27,942
I had a feeling.
Oh. Well, I can't just let you starve!

133
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:42,748
[Zirco and Sapphire chomping]

134
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:47,670
-[father] Oh.
-[chomping continues]

135
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:50,673
You two must not have eaten for some time.

136
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:52,258
While they are welcome here,

137
00:09:52,341 --> 00:09:55,052
maybe next time
you can just bring them the leftovers.

138
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:58,681
Sorry, Mom. I wasn't sure
I could make that kind of decision.

139
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:04,270
I haven't been able to enjoy
a hot meal for so long.

140
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:05,730
I really appreciate it.

141
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:07,148
[girl] Uh, of course.

142
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:10,109
[father] Sounds like food's
been hard to come by.

143
00:10:10,192 --> 00:10:12,945
{\an8}We were forced from our homeland
seven years ago.

144
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:14,822
{\an8}Since then, we couldn't find work,

145
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:16,949
{\an8}so we've been wandering
from place to place,

146
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:18,909
{\an8}eating whatever food we can find.

147
00:10:19,452 --> 00:10:21,287
{\an8}[mother] All too familiar a story.

148
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:23,122
-Awful, nonetheless.
-[father] Mmm.

149
00:10:23,205 --> 00:10:25,875
An old woman and a young girl
all on their own.

150
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:27,335
I imagine it's been rough.

151
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:31,797
It's so good!
This thing is delicious! What is it?

152
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:35,134
[chuckles] That is a bone
in Golden Rat steak.

153
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:38,512
[father] It's one of their
local specialties here in Gold Land.

154
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:40,640
[Sapphire chomping loudly]

155
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:44,518
So this is the Golden Rat steak.
Mmm. I've got room for more!

156
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:47,438
-Can I have another helping? [laughing]
-[mother] I wish I could,

157
00:10:47,521 --> 00:10:49,440
but if you want more, you'll have to pay.

158
00:10:49,523 --> 00:10:51,901
-Times are hard for us, too.
-[Sapphire] Oh, right.

159
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:54,195
Of course.

160
00:10:56,447 --> 00:10:59,200
{\an8}We're willing to do anything.
Please, can we work for you?

161
00:10:59,283 --> 00:11:00,951
{\an8}[father] We've got all the help we need.

162
00:11:01,035 --> 00:11:03,704
{\an8}Do you know anywhere around here
that's looking for workers?

163
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:07,375
In my experience, when outsiders
are looking to make money quickly,

164
00:11:07,458 --> 00:11:09,585
it's the mines that they turn to first.

165
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:11,879
It's not the kind of work I'd recommend.

166
00:11:11,962 --> 00:11:12,963
[Sapphire sighs]

167
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:18,886
I can't just sit around
feeling sorry for myself forever.

168
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:22,223
{\an8}I'll do it.

169
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:24,141
{\an8}Can you take me there?

170
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:26,102
{\an8}What? Now?

171
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:27,603
Uh, um…

172
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:31,023
Don't tell me you're planning to go,
looking like that.

173
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:33,567
[Sapphire and Zirco exclaim]

174
00:11:33,651 --> 00:11:35,611
[father] Fine. Draw them a bath, will you?

175
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:37,405
[both laughing]

176
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:41,617
[Sapphire] <i>I'm Sapphire. Nice to meet you.</i>

177
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:45,079
-[Pine] <i>My name's Pine.</i>
-[Sapphire] <i>Pine? That's such a cute name.</i>

178
00:11:45,162 --> 00:11:46,956
[Pine] <i>Do… Do you really think so?</i>

179
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:50,334
[Sapphire] <i>Originally,</i>
<i>I'm from Silver Land, but…</i>

180
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:54,088
<i>It's a long story,</i>
<i>and kind of a sad one, too,</i>

181
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,923
<i>-but anyway…</i>
-[Pine] <i>I bet it was hard.</i>

182
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:59,009
<i>But now I'm glad to see</i>
<i>that you're doing better.</i>

183
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:01,053
<i>Welcome to Gold Land!</i>

184
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:03,222
[Sapphire chuckles] <i>Thanks.</i>

185
00:12:03,305 --> 00:12:05,391
[bell tolling]

186
00:12:10,646 --> 00:12:13,399
[Velvet] The devastation of Silver Land
suffered like no other,

187
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:16,735
but we've been able to enjoy
relative peace since the calamity.

188
00:12:16,819 --> 00:12:20,448
However, the King of Ash is stirred
and the Nergal are active again.

189
00:12:21,365 --> 00:12:24,452
And as a result, it has slowed
the pace of our mining operation.

190
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:26,328
[man 1] What more can you tell us

191
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:28,998
about the source of crystal energy
discovered the other day?

192
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:32,418
[Velvet] It has been sealed off
and is being investigated.

193
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:35,713
[man 1] Be cautious
that it doesn't provoke the King of Ash.

194
00:12:35,796 --> 00:12:36,630
[Velvet] Understood.

195
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:39,300
[man 2] Our nation's finances
continue to be strained,

196
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:41,677
what with crystal prices
soaring higher than ever.

197
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:44,346
[man 1] And the black market
is only gaining momentum.

198
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:47,016
[Velvet] The miners and immigrants
are becoming agitated.

199
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:50,102
Yesterday they began chanting,
"Defeat the King of Ash" again,

200
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:51,562
which led to another riot.

201
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:54,899
Then suppress them by any means.

202
00:12:55,774 --> 00:12:57,067
{\an8}It is said the Angel of Hope

203
00:12:57,151 --> 00:13:00,362
{\an8}is the only one who can defeat
the King of Ash, is it not?

204
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:02,448
That's a dangerous idea.

205
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:05,784
Any individual caught
disseminating harmful notions,

206
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:08,370
or rumors, will be apprehended at once,

207
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:11,165
and will be subject
to public whipping for their crime.

208
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:12,625
Understood.

209
00:13:13,417 --> 00:13:16,337
[Pope] We must not resist the King of Ash.

210
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:20,090
If we want to survive,
we have no choice but to bear the pain.

211
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:24,637
May the Angel of Hope guide us.

212
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:28,891
[all] May the Angel of Hope guide us.

213
00:13:33,229 --> 00:13:34,355
[Sapphire and Zirco] Mmm.

214
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:36,106
Off we go!

215
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:40,194
You helped me get registered
and everything. Thanks so much.

216
00:13:40,277 --> 00:13:42,655
You'll be starting tomorrow. You ready?

217
00:13:42,738 --> 00:13:43,656
Yeah.

218
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:46,200
{\an8}I've got some business
I have to take care of.

219
00:13:46,283 --> 00:13:48,244
{\an8}Why don't you two go on ahead without me?

220
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:50,204
{\an8}Huh? What business?

221
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:53,040
[Zirco snickers]
You'll just have to wait and see.

222
00:13:53,123 --> 00:13:54,917
Wait, Zirco, that's not fair.

223
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:55,918
[Pine chuckles]

224
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:58,295
Oh, it's nothing.

225
00:13:58,379 --> 00:14:00,798
But there's lots more
interesting stuff over there.

226
00:14:00,881 --> 00:14:02,967
Huh? Really?

227
00:14:04,176 --> 00:14:05,928
-Shall we go?
-Mmm. Yeah.

228
00:14:07,137 --> 00:14:09,890
[laughing]

229
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:12,893
[inhales, sighs]

230
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:18,649
[Pine] <i>Mom, you'd be so proud of me!</i>

231
00:14:18,732 --> 00:14:21,527
<i>I think I might have just made</i>
<i>my first friend.</i>

232
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:23,404
Huh? What's wrong?

233
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:26,365
{\an8}Huh? Really, it's nothing.

234
00:14:26,448 --> 00:14:27,700
Come on. You can tell me.

235
00:14:28,325 --> 00:14:32,162
Look! They're cooking up one of the famous
Golden Rat dishes over there!

236
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:33,747
Huh?! Whoa!

237
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:36,292
[screaming] Did you say "Golden Rat?"

238
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:38,002
Oh, that was close.

239
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:40,296
I'm here all proud of myself
for making a friend,

240
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:42,548
and I don't even know
what Sapphire thinks of me.

241
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:44,800
[Sapphire screams] Where is it?
Where is it?

242
00:14:44,884 --> 00:14:46,093
-Huh?
-[Sapphire] What's that?

243
00:14:46,176 --> 00:14:47,303
Oh, no, not there.

244
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:49,263
[both panting]

245
00:14:58,522 --> 00:14:59,857
{\an8}Why did you do that?

246
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:06,614
[Pine] <i>The stores on the north side</i>
<i>are for upperclass customers only.</i>

247
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:08,699
[Sapphire] <i>Upperclass customers?</i>

248
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:14,872
-How many times do I have to tell you…
-[Sapphire] Oh, I understand.

249
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:18,000
That means outsiders
aren't allowed either.

250
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:19,877
[Pine] What is it?

251
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:22,504
[Sapphire] My country
had stuff like this, too.

252
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:25,341
Not that any of that matters now.

253
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:28,469
The Nergal didn't care about status,
and just destroyed everything.

254
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:30,346
[Pine] Oh, I'm sorry.

255
00:15:30,429 --> 00:15:31,972
[Sapphire] Oh, it's fine, really.

256
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:35,684
Nowadays, it doesn't matter to me
whether someone's upperclass or common.

257
00:15:36,185 --> 00:15:38,270
I just want to try to find
a way to help people.

258
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:41,231
I keep trying to figure out
what I have to offer, though.

259
00:15:41,982 --> 00:15:43,442
Still haven't found it yet.

260
00:15:43,525 --> 00:15:46,070
[Pine] Really? I feel the exact same.

261
00:15:46,153 --> 00:15:48,989
-[Sapphire] Huh?
-There's something inside of me

262
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:50,741
that's always pushing me to help others,

263
00:15:51,241 --> 00:15:53,702
but then I get nervous and I freeze up.

264
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:55,871
I mean, I'm not really good at anything.

265
00:15:56,538 --> 00:15:58,749
What's someone like me even suited for?

266
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:03,087
Pine, you're just like me, then.

267
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:05,673
{\an8}I'm not like you at all.

268
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:08,467
{\an8}Your home country fell apart,

269
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:10,886
{\an8}but that didn't stop you
from surviving on your own.

270
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:13,472
{\an8}You're amazing. I could never do that.

271
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:15,683
{\an8}I can barely do anything.

272
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:17,977
{\an8}I'm hardly amazing.

273
00:16:18,477 --> 00:16:21,105
I mean, I still haven't helped anybody.

274
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:23,941
I have an idea.

275
00:16:24,608 --> 00:16:26,902
Let's try and find something
we can do together.

276
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:30,698
But if that's the case,
then you're gonna have to be my friend.

277
00:16:30,781 --> 00:16:33,158
[gasps] Friends?

278
00:16:33,242 --> 00:16:36,578
[Sapphire] F-R-I-E-N-D-S.
Friends. [chuckles]

279
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:41,625
[Zirco] <i>Sapphire! I found a place</i>
<i>where we can stay!</i>

280
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:45,004
[Sapphire] <i>Wow, really?</i>
<i>Thank you so much, Zirco.</i>

281
00:16:46,672 --> 00:16:49,174
-Hey, Zirco?
-[Zirco] What is it, Sapphire?

282
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:53,137
I made a friend who's my age
for the first time.

283
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:55,639
Mmm. Did you, now?

284
00:16:56,181 --> 00:16:58,809
[breathing deeply]

285
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:02,229
[Zirco] Asleep already, are you?

286
00:17:03,105 --> 00:17:05,232
I'm happy for you, Sapphire.

287
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:08,277
[bell tolling]

288
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,486
[groans softly]

289
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,447
[both gargle]

290
00:17:15,117 --> 00:17:17,369
[bell continues tolling]

291
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:31,717
[Rock] All right, guys.

292
00:17:32,551 --> 00:17:35,054
Sapphire and Zirco here
will be joining our group.

293
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:36,638
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

294
00:17:36,722 --> 00:17:38,766
My name is Rock, and I'm the leader.

295
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:40,726
This is Chorogy,

296
00:17:40,809 --> 00:17:42,436
-and next to him is Hecate.
-[scoffs]

297
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:46,607
{\an8}-My name is Chick.
-And my name is Tack.

298
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:48,442
[Sapphire] You guys look exactly alike.

299
00:17:48,525 --> 00:17:51,653
[Chorogy] Sheesh. So they finally decided
to send us reinforcements,

300
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:53,947
and what do we get? An old lady.

301
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:55,532
[Rock] Hey, come on, Chorogy.

302
00:17:55,616 --> 00:17:57,201
[Zirco chuckles] Even old ladies

303
00:17:57,284 --> 00:17:59,536
have to work
for their food somehow, you know.

304
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:00,829
-[punches]
-[groans]

305
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:03,207
-[workers clamoring]
-Right, now restrain him.

306
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:09,129
You were the one who was leading that riot
the other day, weren't you?

307
00:18:09,213 --> 00:18:11,090
Ugh. Damn it all.

308
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:14,259
Why are we the ones always forced
to do the dangerous work?

309
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:17,429
Come on, everyone!
Raise the rallying cry! Fight!

310
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:21,683
Are you finished with your ranting now?

311
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:23,852
You have us scraping to the King of Ash,

312
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:26,814
when that Nergal's just going
to kill us all eventually!

313
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:29,191
But you Mitra just sit and watch!

314
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:31,318
You bastards think you can--

315
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:33,320
-[punch lands]
-[groaning]

316
00:18:33,403 --> 00:18:35,280
Throw him in solitary. Take him away.

317
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,285
Let me remind you all of the rules here.

318
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:42,996
No one must ever defy the King of Ash!

319
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:46,250
Instead, be grateful to the King of Ash
that you remain alive.

320
00:18:46,750 --> 00:18:48,001
Now get back to work!

321
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:50,129
May the Angel of Hope guide us.

322
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:52,965
[Rock] Velvet, that bastard.

323
00:18:53,048 --> 00:18:54,007
[Sapphire] Who's he?

324
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:56,927
[Rock] One of the Mitra in charge
of managing the mining site.

325
00:18:58,053 --> 00:19:00,139
[Sapphire] I can tell
I don't like him already.

326
00:19:00,222 --> 00:19:02,724
[Rock] Trust me, it'd be best
if you don't do anything

327
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:04,226
to draw his attention.

328
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:13,360
So, how much of this crystal
should I be digging up?

329
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:15,070
As much as you can.

330
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:17,614
The more crystals you unearth,
the more you get paid.

331
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:20,409
More crystals means more money? [yelps]

332
00:19:20,492 --> 00:19:23,579
There's a little Golden Rat steak
with my name on it.

333
00:19:23,662 --> 00:19:25,956
Moron. You make it sound like it's easy.

334
00:19:26,039 --> 00:19:27,666
What do you mean by "Moron"?

335
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:31,044
Come on, newbie.
There's no beginner's luck on this job.

336
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:33,839
I don't need luck. I've got skill.

337
00:19:33,922 --> 00:19:36,091
All right, then,
if you dig up more than I do,

338
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:39,261
-you can have my whole share.
-[screams] Really?

339
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:45,809
[Sapphire] All right, crystals.
Come to mama!

340
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:46,977
Huh?

341
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:49,313
-[effort screaming]
-She's really giving it her all.

342
00:19:49,396 --> 00:19:52,482
She'll wear herself out like that.
Come on. There's a better spot there.

343
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:59,406
-[Chick] What's with that machine?
-[Tack] She's cheating. Not fair.

344
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:02,201
[Zirco] I may not look it,
but this old lady is a genius inventor.

345
00:20:03,493 --> 00:20:06,872
[Hecate and Chorogy] One, two. One, two.
One, two. One, two. One, two. One, two.

346
00:20:06,955 --> 00:20:08,332
[Rock sighs]

347
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:11,877
Nice work today, guys.
We might even finish early.

348
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,837
[Sapphire] One, two.
One steak, two steaks.

349
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:17,216
One steak, two steaks. Two steaks for me!

350
00:20:17,966 --> 00:20:19,676
[Chorogy] Is her yield increasing?

351
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,428
Focus on your own work.

352
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:23,639
Why do you turn everything
into a competition?

353
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:25,432
And how did I get involved?

354
00:20:25,515 --> 00:20:27,517
Could you be more annoying?

355
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:30,020
[rat squealing]

356
00:20:30,103 --> 00:20:34,483
[screaming]

357
00:20:35,067 --> 00:20:36,610
What do you think you're doing?!

358
00:20:36,693 --> 00:20:38,946
Sorry. I didn't do it on purpose.

359
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:43,867
That's a bad sign.

360
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:48,914
-[explosion]
-[gasps] Huh?

361
00:20:53,835 --> 00:20:55,629
[grunts, pants]

362
00:20:59,132 --> 00:21:01,009
[gasps] A Nergal?

363
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:05,389
<i>But wait, it doesn't look like the one</i>
<i>that came to Silver Land.</i>

364
00:21:10,519 --> 00:21:12,229
[clamoring in distance]

365
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:15,524
The Nergal's back again.

366
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:18,110
Yes, sir. Lord Velvet,
you should evacuate, too.

367
00:21:18,193 --> 00:21:21,029
Get as many of the remaining miners
as possible to safety.

368
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:24,157
I'm afraid we can't afford
to lose any more workers.

369
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:25,284
[both guards] Yes, sir.

370
00:21:27,327 --> 00:21:29,705
-[people screaming]
-[man] Quickly! Keep moving!

371
00:21:30,747 --> 00:21:31,999
-You, don't stop!
-[guard] Move!

372
00:21:32,082 --> 00:21:34,626
{\an8}-Get yourself to higher ground! Quickly!
-[guard] Keep moving!

373
00:21:36,169 --> 00:21:38,171
{\an8}-[woman 1] Are you all right?
-[man panting]

374
00:21:38,255 --> 00:21:39,089
{\an8}[woman 2] Hurry up!

375
00:21:47,931 --> 00:21:50,017
[wailing]

376
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:53,145
[sighs] This is all my fault.

377
00:21:53,228 --> 00:21:55,731
[Rock] Forget about that for now.
We gotta run.

378
00:21:56,732 --> 00:21:58,692
Can't we do something
other than running away?

379
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:03,071
[man gasps]

380
00:22:08,577 --> 00:22:10,537
[screaming]

381
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:11,955
-[Rock] Newbie!
-Oh, no!

382
00:22:15,542 --> 00:22:17,419
[continues screaming]

383
00:22:24,009 --> 00:22:26,428
[Zirco] Oh, no. Sapphire! Sapphire!

384
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:32,392
Sapphire! Where are you? Sapphire!

385
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:33,393
[groans]

386
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:40,150
Oh, I'm sorry I didn't see you there.
You better get going.

387
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:41,151
See ya.

388
00:22:41,777 --> 00:22:43,653
[Tack groaning]

389
00:22:45,530 --> 00:22:46,615
[whimpers]

390
00:22:53,538 --> 00:22:54,998
Here. Hold on.

391
00:22:56,041 --> 00:22:56,917
Thanks, lady.

392
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:00,420
[both gasp]

393
00:23:08,053 --> 00:23:10,263
[both voices shaking] We… We're done for.

394
00:23:14,184 --> 00:23:15,185
[Zirco yelps]

395
00:23:15,268 --> 00:23:17,479
[all screaming]

396
00:23:31,368 --> 00:23:33,870
-You gotta be kidding.
-What about Tack?

397
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:41,962
[lullaby music playing]

398
00:23:56,518 --> 00:23:58,395
[Sapphire] <i>After losing everything,</i>

399
00:24:00,814 --> 00:24:05,360
<i>being disposed of,</i>
<i>left all alone, I couldn't do anything.</i>

400
00:24:06,111 --> 00:24:07,779
<i>And now I just die here?</i>

401
00:24:08,363 --> 00:24:10,740
[Queen] <i>Trying to fight</i>
<i>against this world is meaningless.</i>

402
00:24:11,449 --> 00:24:13,368
<i>Why can't you understand that?</i>

403
00:24:14,244 --> 00:24:16,580
[Sapphire] <i>No,</i>
<i>I can't let it end like this.</i>

404
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:19,166
<i>I haven't gotten anything back!</i>

405
00:24:28,592 --> 00:24:31,219
[banging]

406
00:24:37,434 --> 00:24:39,769
[captivating music playing]

407
00:25:22,103 --> 00:25:24,731
[music intensifies]

408
00:25:38,161 --> 00:25:40,121
Huh? What's all this?

409
00:25:40,205 --> 00:25:41,623
[groaning]

410
00:25:43,124 --> 00:25:44,334
Hecate!

411
00:25:46,127 --> 00:25:47,754
[whimpering]

412
00:25:47,837 --> 00:25:49,256
[Sapphire] Look out!

413
00:25:49,339 --> 00:25:50,465
[Sapphire screaming]

414
00:26:01,810 --> 00:26:05,438
[groans] What?! Was that really me?!

415
00:26:05,522 --> 00:26:08,566
{\an8}-The new girl?
-Sapphire, there you are!

416
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:09,943
{\an8}What's going on?

417
00:26:10,026 --> 00:26:11,903
What is she doing?

418
00:26:11,987 --> 00:26:13,405
Who is this girl?

419
00:26:13,488 --> 00:26:16,324
[Sapphire] Hey, guys!
Get away while you can!

420
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:24,207
[exclaims] Whoa!

421
00:26:27,752 --> 00:26:30,130
[panting] Over there!

422
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:35,927
I've got this.

423
00:26:44,102 --> 00:26:46,813
Ha! [grunts, strains]

424
00:26:50,859 --> 00:26:53,528
[Nergal roars]

425
00:26:57,490 --> 00:26:59,909
[effort scream]

426
00:27:04,289 --> 00:27:06,416
Yahoo! [laughs]

427
00:27:09,502 --> 00:27:10,545
[laughs]

428
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:14,758
Huh? Cool!

429
00:27:15,425 --> 00:27:16,468
[horse neighs]

430
00:27:22,307 --> 00:27:23,933
Let's get you out of here.

431
00:27:24,017 --> 00:27:26,311
[Nergal growling]

432
00:27:31,274 --> 00:27:32,108
[man groans]

433
00:27:32,192 --> 00:27:34,569
Oh, no. It's headed this way.

434
00:27:34,652 --> 00:27:36,154
They're in trouble. [grunts]

435
00:27:42,702 --> 00:27:44,079
{\an8}What do I do now?

436
00:27:58,301 --> 00:28:01,096
-[Rock] She's not affected by the mold?
-[Chick] Incredible.

437
00:28:01,179 --> 00:28:03,181
She's like a knight or something.

438
00:28:03,264 --> 00:28:04,307
Sapphire!

439
00:28:04,391 --> 00:28:06,059
[both] You can do it!

440
00:28:06,142 --> 00:28:07,560
[chuckles]

441
00:28:08,395 --> 00:28:10,688
Everyone, I'm so sorry.

442
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:13,316
[woman] What's going on down there?
Something's strange.

443
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:15,068
[man] Is someone fighting it?

444
00:28:15,151 --> 00:28:15,985
Huh?

445
00:28:17,529 --> 00:28:18,988
What's happening?

446
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:22,367
Someone's actually fighting
one of the Nergal?

447
00:28:22,992 --> 00:28:25,995
I doubt we'll be able to use
this mining site after this.

448
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:29,791
But we do have this guy's team
to thank for saving us. [chuckles]

449
00:28:31,251 --> 00:28:33,503
[straining]

450
00:28:50,937 --> 00:28:53,189
[screaming]

451
00:28:57,444 --> 00:28:58,528
[gasps]

452
00:28:59,821 --> 00:29:01,239
Well, that's no help.

453
00:29:03,783 --> 00:29:04,743
What do I do?

454
00:29:06,661 --> 00:29:07,912
Huh? What's this?

455
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:12,792
This should work.

456
00:29:13,877 --> 00:29:15,754
[dramatic music playing]

457
00:29:21,551 --> 00:29:24,471
[effort scream]

458
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:40,737
[cheering]

459
00:29:43,782 --> 00:29:44,949
[scoffs]

460
00:29:45,033 --> 00:29:47,911
{\an8}The Princess Knight to the rescue.

461
00:29:58,338 --> 00:30:01,007
[Nergal wailing]

462
00:30:09,224 --> 00:30:11,768
Is the Nergal really running away?

463
00:30:11,851 --> 00:30:13,102
I don't believe it.

464
00:30:13,186 --> 00:30:15,104
Whoa! It's running away!

465
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:17,148
-It's retreating!
-[exclaims] Hooray!

466
00:30:17,232 --> 00:30:19,609
[all cheering]

467
00:30:24,113 --> 00:30:26,658
[guard] You're saying
that the Nergal ran away?

468
00:30:26,741 --> 00:30:28,743
[Velvet] Which team was present? Tell me.

469
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:32,288
Yes, sir. The team I saw the closest to it
down there was Rock's crew.

470
00:30:32,372 --> 00:30:33,665
Isn't that right, Chorogy?

471
00:30:33,748 --> 00:30:36,000
Yes, it's exactly as he said.

472
00:30:36,918 --> 00:30:39,754
Could this be the work
of a demon, or was it…

473
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:40,672
-Mmm?
-No.

474
00:30:41,714 --> 00:30:44,717
-Bring Rock's crew to me at once!
-[guard 1] Yes, sir.

475
00:30:44,801 --> 00:30:46,678
Count the miners and check for casualties,

476
00:30:46,761 --> 00:30:49,013
-and tend to the injured!
-[guard 2] Yes, sir!

477
00:30:50,390 --> 00:30:52,767
[Queen] <i>This whole world</i>
<i>can perish and rot.</i>

478
00:30:53,726 --> 00:30:56,062
<i>But my final wish is that you live on.</i>

479
00:30:57,897 --> 00:31:00,108
Good boy. Thanks for all your help.

480
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:01,609
[chuckles]

481
00:31:04,821 --> 00:31:07,824
So, how do I… How does this thing work?

482
00:31:08,449 --> 00:31:12,787
Come on!
There's gotta be a switch or something!

483
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:13,788
[gasps]

484
00:31:15,123 --> 00:31:16,291
Oh. [gasps]

485
00:31:17,083 --> 00:31:18,877
{\an8}-Well, that did it.
-[people approaching]

486
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:20,253
{\an8}At least it's over for now.

487
00:31:20,336 --> 00:31:21,671
{\an8}-[Tack] There!
-[Zirco] I see her!

488
00:31:23,298 --> 00:31:25,216
{\an8}-[Sapphire] Oh, you're safe.
-Sapphire!

489
00:31:25,300 --> 00:31:27,635
-[Chick] Thank you.
-[Tack] Thank you so much.

490
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:29,304
Are you all right, sapphire?

491
00:31:29,387 --> 00:31:32,974
-You're not hurt, are you?
-No, but I am a bit…

492
00:31:33,933 --> 00:31:35,310
A bit tired.

493
00:31:35,393 --> 00:31:36,728
-[all gasp]
-[Zirco] Sapphire!

494
00:31:36,811 --> 00:31:41,190
[crying] I'm sorry. So sorry, Sapphire.
I'm the one who was a moron.

495
00:31:43,276 --> 00:31:44,903
What are you crying about?

496
00:31:44,986 --> 00:31:48,781
Sapphire, you're amazing. I mean it.

497
00:31:48,865 --> 00:31:52,660
{\an8}[sobbing] I'm gonna give you
all of my crystals!

498
00:31:52,744 --> 00:31:54,495
[Sapphire] I don't need all that, Hecate.

499
00:31:55,246 --> 00:31:56,664
But how about this?

500
00:32:05,173 --> 00:32:06,424
[chuckles]

501
00:32:08,426 --> 00:32:09,594
[all laughing]

502
00:32:11,888 --> 00:32:13,973
[electrical buzzing]

503
00:32:17,644 --> 00:32:20,021
[indistinct talking]

504
00:32:27,737 --> 00:32:29,614
[Rock] Well, we didn't see
anyone like that.

505
00:32:33,493 --> 00:32:35,286
Clearly, someone is responsible.

506
00:32:36,037 --> 00:32:39,123
If you're caught lying to me,
the punishment is death.

507
00:32:39,207 --> 00:32:40,124
Death?

508
00:32:41,250 --> 00:32:43,461
{\an8}Once the King of Ash has been provoked,

509
00:32:43,544 --> 00:32:46,547
{\an8}the Nergal will return
to destroy us completely.

510
00:32:47,173 --> 00:32:49,425
{\an8}Which means your jobs
are on the line as well.

511
00:32:49,509 --> 00:32:52,470
That Nergal tripped on its own tail,
bit its tongue,

512
00:32:52,553 --> 00:32:54,722
-and scurried off whimpering.
-[Velvet] Enough.

513
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:56,015
Uh, you know…

514
00:32:56,099 --> 00:32:58,309
-[Velvet] What is it?
-Actually… [groans]

515
00:32:58,393 --> 00:33:00,269
Your threats will get you nowhere.

516
00:33:02,105 --> 00:33:02,939
{\an8}Fine, then.

517
00:33:03,481 --> 00:33:05,984
{\an8}But should you notice anything,
I expect a report.

518
00:33:06,067 --> 00:33:09,404
[Rock] Indeed, if we do,
we'll let you know.

519
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:17,578
Listen up. I won't have
any of us selling out our own.

520
00:33:18,204 --> 00:33:22,458
We don't know anything about the person
who fought that Nergal, understand?

521
00:33:22,542 --> 00:33:23,876
I appreciate it.

522
00:33:25,420 --> 00:33:26,796
[guard 1] Sir, what do you think?

523
00:33:27,338 --> 00:33:28,673
Were they telling the truth?

524
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:33,219
{\an8}What happened here today
is strictly confidential.

525
00:33:33,302 --> 00:33:34,637
{\an8}It does not leave this room.

526
00:33:34,721 --> 00:33:37,015
{\an8}-[guard 1] But, sir--
-I'm serious.

527
00:33:37,098 --> 00:33:39,392
{\an8}And I will take
full responsibility for it.

528
00:33:41,894 --> 00:33:43,771
[Rock] To our safe return!

529
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:45,481
[all] Cheers!

530
00:33:45,565 --> 00:33:47,442
-[Pine's father] Take this.
-Sure.

531
00:33:47,525 --> 00:33:49,986
[Hecate] Tonight, drinks are on me!

532
00:33:50,069 --> 00:33:52,905
[all cheering]

533
00:33:52,989 --> 00:33:55,450
[Pine] Sorry for the wait, Sapphire.
Here's your favorite.

534
00:33:55,533 --> 00:33:57,410
[exclaims]

535
00:33:58,077 --> 00:34:00,496
Come on, Pine, you too.
Let's have a toast.

536
00:34:00,580 --> 00:34:02,707
Huh? All right. Cheers.

537
00:34:02,790 --> 00:34:04,167
[both chuckle]

538
00:34:04,250 --> 00:34:06,377
Mmm. [satisfied sigh]

539
00:34:06,919 --> 00:34:08,963
I've been waiting for you, Golden Rat.

540
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:10,214
It's so good.

541
00:34:10,965 --> 00:34:13,760
I wish I could stay,
but I have to help the other customers.

542
00:34:13,843 --> 00:34:15,386
Sorry, I don't want to keep you.

543
00:34:15,470 --> 00:34:18,806
I just wanted to make sure
I shared some of this joy with you, Pine.

544
00:34:18,890 --> 00:34:20,433
Oh, don't apologize.

545
00:34:20,516 --> 00:34:22,935
I've been so busy,
I'm the one who should say sorry.

546
00:34:23,019 --> 00:34:25,772
When I heard a Nergal had appeared again,
I was so surprised.

547
00:34:25,855 --> 00:34:27,106
[exclaims] You know?

548
00:34:27,690 --> 00:34:30,568
In all honesty, I wasn't sure
I was gonna make it.

549
00:34:30,651 --> 00:34:33,529
But everyone is talking about
how amazing you were.

550
00:34:33,613 --> 00:34:35,073
[laughs]

551
00:34:35,156 --> 00:34:36,741
It was luck. That's all.

552
00:34:36,824 --> 00:34:38,034
-[Pine's father] Pine!
-Oh.

553
00:34:38,117 --> 00:34:40,078
Uh, hey, Sapphire.

554
00:34:40,161 --> 00:34:42,747
I've been thinking about
what I can do to help people, too.

555
00:34:42,830 --> 00:34:45,541
Ta-da! I wanna share my ideas with you!

556
00:34:46,250 --> 00:34:48,377
Really? I love that.

557
00:34:48,461 --> 00:34:50,004
I better get back to work.

558
00:34:50,088 --> 00:34:51,506
[Sapphire] You got this.

559
00:34:52,131 --> 00:34:53,216
[sighs]

560
00:34:53,299 --> 00:34:56,302
[Endo] It's wild, though,
because if it weren't for that knight,

561
00:34:56,385 --> 00:34:57,970
there wouldn't be this many survivors.

562
00:34:58,054 --> 00:35:00,556
[man] Quiet. Rock told us
not to talk about that.

563
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:02,850
[Endo] It's fine. We're celebrating today.

564
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:05,645
We're letting loose. So what if our lips
get loose, too? [laughs]

565
00:35:05,728 --> 00:35:07,605
[Sembry] Oh, dear knight,
oh, Angel of Hope,

566
00:35:07,688 --> 00:35:10,149
please eliminate all the Nergal for us!

567
00:35:11,317 --> 00:35:13,945
-[Chorogy] What are you talking about?
-What's wrong with you?

568
00:35:14,487 --> 00:35:17,573
[Chorogy] The Mitra are always saying
that if you anger the King of Ash,

569
00:35:17,657 --> 00:35:19,242
terrible things will happen.

570
00:35:19,325 --> 00:35:21,369
Now, wait a second. Last time I checked,

571
00:35:21,452 --> 00:35:22,995
you're an immigrant too, Chorogy.

572
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:25,206
Now you're gonna side
with the Gold Landers?

573
00:35:25,289 --> 00:35:27,750
We lied to them.
If they find out, they'll kill us.

574
00:35:27,834 --> 00:35:28,918
[Sembry] Shut your mouth.

575
00:35:29,001 --> 00:35:31,879
And why should I?
I haven't said anything wrong!

576
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:34,924
-[Sembry] You've got more to say?
-[Rock] That's enough, Chorogy.

577
00:35:35,424 --> 00:35:38,845
Tonight, all the drinks are on me,
so no fighting.

578
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:42,932
Sorry about getting you dragged
into this, Chorogy.

579
00:35:43,015 --> 00:35:44,684
-[Chorogy grunts]
-[Rock] Wait.

580
00:35:48,855 --> 00:35:50,523
[sighs] What's his problem?

581
00:35:51,107 --> 00:35:53,651
Whatever. Let's party!

582
00:35:53,734 --> 00:35:54,610
[all] Yeah!

583
00:35:55,444 --> 00:35:57,530
[Pine humming]

584
00:36:05,079 --> 00:36:06,330
It's not fair.

585
00:36:06,414 --> 00:36:10,543
You give Sapphire a little attention,
and suddenly she's all full of herself

586
00:36:10,626 --> 00:36:12,962
just because she took out
one of the Nergal.

587
00:36:13,045 --> 00:36:14,297
[man] Hey, you.

588
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:16,174
[Chorogy groaning]

589
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:21,596
[Chorogy screaming]

590
00:36:23,556 --> 00:36:26,100
[Zirco] I must say, that thing
came as quite a surprise.

591
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:27,518
What thing?

592
00:36:27,602 --> 00:36:30,313
That thing you're wearing
on your head, Sapphire.

593
00:36:30,396 --> 00:36:32,231
Uh, my ribbon?

594
00:36:32,315 --> 00:36:35,234
Mmm. I'd like to take
a closer look at that thing.

595
00:36:35,318 --> 00:36:36,485
[straining]

596
00:36:40,198 --> 00:36:41,699
Why isn't it doing it?

597
00:36:41,782 --> 00:36:43,743
[Zirco] Are you trying
to keep me in suspense?

598
00:36:43,826 --> 00:36:45,620
[straining]

599
00:36:51,584 --> 00:36:52,710
Ooh!

600
00:36:52,793 --> 00:36:55,630
{\an8}I think maybe it has something
to do with the crystals.

601
00:36:55,713 --> 00:36:58,466
{\an8}Hmm. If I'm honest,
I don't really understand it myself.

602
00:36:59,091 --> 00:37:01,385
{\an8}And your body feels perfectly fine, right?

603
00:37:02,136 --> 00:37:03,596
Mmm, yeah. I feel great.

604
00:37:04,889 --> 00:37:06,265
Maybe even better than ever.

605
00:37:06,807 --> 00:37:09,143
{\an8}[sighs in relief] I'm glad to hear it.

606
00:37:10,102 --> 00:37:11,479
[sobs softly]

607
00:37:11,562 --> 00:37:14,607
It must have been scary.
I'm so proud of you, Sapphire.

608
00:37:16,025 --> 00:37:18,319
{\an8}There's nothing you can do to stop it.

609
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:21,364
It's over, accept it.

610
00:37:23,616 --> 00:37:25,743
Hey, Zirco, I found it.

611
00:37:25,826 --> 00:37:28,371
I know what I want to do.
I know what my purpose is.

612
00:37:28,996 --> 00:37:30,581
-[Zirco] Helping people?
-Mmm.

613
00:37:31,540 --> 00:37:34,627
But it's more than just fighting Nergal
as the Princess Knight.

614
00:37:34,710 --> 00:37:37,296
Anyone who's been struggling
deserves my help.

615
00:37:37,380 --> 00:37:39,966
And I think I survived
to be that kind of hero.

616
00:37:41,175 --> 00:37:42,385
{\an8}And I'm your support.

617
00:37:42,468 --> 00:37:45,429
{\an8}If there's anything
you need this genius inventor to make,

618
00:37:45,513 --> 00:37:46,847
{\an8}you let me know.

619
00:37:46,931 --> 00:37:48,557
Mmm. Thanks, Zirco.

620
00:37:49,892 --> 00:37:51,727
Hmm? Actually…

621
00:37:57,900 --> 00:37:59,819
[pleasant music playing]

622
00:38:23,676 --> 00:38:25,011
[man 1] Oh, dear.

623
00:38:25,094 --> 00:38:28,055
The fire is spreading faster
than they can put it out. What's that?

624
00:38:28,139 --> 00:38:30,433
Is that the cry of someone
who's been left behind?

625
00:38:30,516 --> 00:38:31,600
What will they do now?

626
00:38:32,685 --> 00:38:36,188
[man 2] Princess Knight to the rescue!
Alley-oop!

627
00:38:37,148 --> 00:38:40,318
[man 1] And just like that,
the young girl was rescued.

628
00:38:42,111 --> 00:38:43,571
[man 1] I saw that in real life.

629
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:45,406
[woman] She was incredible, wasn't she?

630
00:38:45,489 --> 00:38:47,742
[man 2] The Princess Knight
appeared again, huh?

631
00:38:47,825 --> 00:38:50,036
[man 1] You know,
she saved my life once, too.

632
00:38:50,119 --> 00:38:51,078
[chuckles]

633
00:39:00,087 --> 00:39:01,464
[Pine] Ta-da!

634
00:39:02,214 --> 00:39:05,426
I'm still not sure
what exactly I can do to help people,

635
00:39:05,509 --> 00:39:08,304
but I started by writing down
the things that I'm good at.

636
00:39:08,387 --> 00:39:09,930
Oh. Like what?

637
00:39:10,681 --> 00:39:12,641
The first one I wrote down is singing.

638
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:16,937
-Wow, Pine, I love it!
-Welp, I actually said it out loud.

639
00:39:17,021 --> 00:39:18,481
Then this will be perfect.

640
00:39:18,564 --> 00:39:19,815
Uh? [screams]

641
00:39:19,899 --> 00:39:21,275
[Sapphire] Ta-da!

642
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:23,235
[gasps loudly] What have you got?

643
00:39:24,070 --> 00:39:26,155
[flute playing]

644
00:39:26,822 --> 00:39:30,076
-It's a flute.
-[exclaims]

645
00:39:30,159 --> 00:39:33,829
I was right.
Something told me you loved music.

646
00:39:33,913 --> 00:39:35,039
Why wouldn't you?

647
00:39:35,122 --> 00:39:37,917
Music has the ability
to lift people's spirits.

648
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:41,212
[chuckles] Yeah. Exactly.

649
00:39:41,295 --> 00:39:44,507
-Why don't we give it a try right now?
-Sure.

650
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:48,386
[Pine] <i>♪ Long, long ago ♪</i>

651
00:39:48,469 --> 00:39:51,347
<i>♪ There was a lone girl ♪</i>

652
00:39:51,430 --> 00:39:54,642
<i>♪ Who wandered the land ♪</i>

653
00:39:54,725 --> 00:40:00,272
<i>♪ Winter-worn and hungry ♪</i>

654
00:40:00,356 --> 00:40:02,233
-[footsteps approaching]
-Uh.

655
00:40:05,486 --> 00:40:06,362
Huh.

656
00:40:07,113 --> 00:40:09,281
You're that miner, Sapphire, aren't you?

657
00:40:09,365 --> 00:40:10,741
Yeah, that's right.

658
00:40:10,825 --> 00:40:12,201
[foreboding music playing]

659
00:40:27,842 --> 00:40:29,677
[grunts]

660
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:30,636
What do you want?

661
00:40:30,719 --> 00:40:32,471
Why have you brought me here?

662
00:40:36,475 --> 00:40:38,811
[intense music playing]

663
00:40:38,894 --> 00:40:42,064
[both grunting]

664
00:40:51,198 --> 00:40:52,241
[yelps]

665
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:03,127
[gasping]

666
00:41:07,882 --> 00:41:09,550
[Velvet] So you're this Ribbon Demon?

667
00:41:11,886 --> 00:41:14,555
That power of yours, where did you get it?

668
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:17,850
A power that can even defeat a Nergal.

669
00:41:18,392 --> 00:41:20,352
Did you undergo some kind
of special training?

670
00:41:20,936 --> 00:41:22,855
How is it that you're unaffected
by the mold?

671
00:41:22,938 --> 00:41:25,774
-[Sapphire] I don't know.
-Answer me. Don't pretend to be stupid.

672
00:41:25,858 --> 00:41:27,234
But I'm telling the truth.

673
00:41:27,318 --> 00:41:30,404
I accidentally fell into a glowing pool
at the mining site,

674
00:41:30,488 --> 00:41:32,740
and the power
just started flowing out of me.

675
00:41:32,823 --> 00:41:34,492
Are you saying it was the crystals?

676
00:41:34,575 --> 00:41:38,704
The body cannot survive that potent
an influx of concentrated photon energy.

677
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:41,165
You're an immigrant.

678
00:41:41,749 --> 00:41:43,000
What country are you from?

679
00:41:43,834 --> 00:41:45,503
I come from Silver Land.

680
00:41:45,586 --> 00:41:47,713
[scoffs] Silver Land, huh?

681
00:41:47,796 --> 00:41:48,964
It's all destroyed now.

682
00:41:49,048 --> 00:41:50,966
I know who you are.

683
00:41:51,592 --> 00:41:53,928
You are the… The cursed princess.

684
00:41:54,011 --> 00:41:55,012
[gasps]

685
00:41:55,095 --> 00:41:58,557
You bear the responsibility
for the destruction of Silver Land.

686
00:42:00,476 --> 00:42:02,019
You escaped your destiny.

687
00:42:02,686 --> 00:42:04,813
Even if it meant the destruction
of your kingdom,

688
00:42:04,897 --> 00:42:06,315
the queen wouldn't let you die.

689
00:42:07,107 --> 00:42:09,360
How profoundly deep a mother's love is.

690
00:42:09,860 --> 00:42:12,696
[Sapphire] Wait a moment.
I don't understand anything you're saying.

691
00:42:13,197 --> 00:42:14,490
[Velvet] You really don't know?

692
00:42:15,491 --> 00:42:17,326
Nergals feed on pure souls.

693
00:42:18,327 --> 00:42:22,164
Had the proper sacrifices been made,
your kingdom could have avoided ruin.

694
00:42:23,582 --> 00:42:25,209
In the country of Silver Land,

695
00:42:25,292 --> 00:42:28,128
it is the pure soul of the princess
that has given as an offering.

696
00:42:29,505 --> 00:42:31,799
-You mean me?
-Precisely.

697
00:42:31,882 --> 00:42:34,301
But your mother, the Queen,
would not allow it.

698
00:42:34,927 --> 00:42:37,388
And as a result, your home was destroyed.

699
00:42:37,930 --> 00:42:41,350
You could even say you destroyed it,
Princess Sapphire.

700
00:42:41,433 --> 00:42:42,726
That can't be.

701
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:44,228
I would never.

702
00:42:45,729 --> 00:42:49,984
You bear a curse, and now you want
to unleash it in our land?

703
00:42:50,067 --> 00:42:51,860
To bring Gold Land to ruin?

704
00:42:51,944 --> 00:42:54,405
Provoking the King of Ash
will bring nothing else.

705
00:42:55,114 --> 00:42:56,657
But the power of this ribbon,

706
00:42:57,241 --> 00:42:59,076
it can defeat the Nergal.

707
00:42:59,159 --> 00:43:02,871
I'm trying to tell you that power
will prove nothing but a calamity.

708
00:43:02,955 --> 00:43:04,540
No one asked you to intervene.

709
00:43:04,623 --> 00:43:06,834
[breath trembling] All the same,

710
00:43:07,501 --> 00:43:09,461
this power must be useful somehow.

711
00:43:11,088 --> 00:43:12,673
So why don't you help me?

712
00:43:13,173 --> 00:43:15,217
How am I supposed to break my curse?

713
00:43:16,260 --> 00:43:18,971
How was it done if not by fighting?

714
00:43:33,027 --> 00:43:33,944
[yawns]

715
00:43:35,404 --> 00:43:37,281
-[panting, exclaims]
-Ow!

716
00:43:37,364 --> 00:43:42,036
{\an8}[groans] Come on, Chorogy.
Can't you watch where you're going, bozo?

717
00:43:42,661 --> 00:43:44,997
-[groans]
-I'm sorry. I gotta--

718
00:43:45,080 --> 00:43:46,707
You're not going anywhere.

719
00:43:46,790 --> 00:43:49,960
Where have you been?
You've been slacking off work all week!

720
00:43:50,044 --> 00:43:52,171
Something smells fishy.

721
00:43:58,552 --> 00:44:02,056
[Pine] <i>Why didn't I say anything?</i>
<i>Why didn't I try to stop them?</i>

722
00:44:02,973 --> 00:44:04,308
<i>I'm the worst friend ever.</i>

723
00:44:04,391 --> 00:44:06,477
[Zirco sighs] Quite the haul today.

724
00:44:07,811 --> 00:44:10,856
-Zirco.
-Oh. Is something the matter, Pine?

725
00:44:10,939 --> 00:44:12,399
I think she's in trouble!

726
00:44:12,483 --> 00:44:14,943
The Mitra came
and they took Sapphire away by force.

727
00:44:15,027 --> 00:44:17,237
-The Mitra?!
-[Hecate] If you want to know the details,

728
00:44:17,321 --> 00:44:19,114
-you can ask him.
-[groans]

729
00:44:19,198 --> 00:44:22,284
Because he's the one who sold out
Sapphire's secret to Velvet

730
00:44:22,368 --> 00:44:23,243
and the Mitra.

731
00:44:24,078 --> 00:44:26,413
[Pine] Sapphire's secret?
What do you mean?

732
00:44:27,039 --> 00:44:30,042
The one who defeated the Nergal,
the Princess Knight is…

733
00:44:30,626 --> 00:44:32,878
Well, her real identity is Sapphire.

734
00:44:33,462 --> 00:44:34,838
Quiet! Zirco!

735
00:44:36,465 --> 00:44:38,342
But how did the two of you know about it?

736
00:44:38,425 --> 00:44:41,136
I only know because she saved my life,

737
00:44:41,220 --> 00:44:43,806
which is exactly what she did
for this slimy idiot.

738
00:44:43,889 --> 00:44:45,307
And yet he still ratted her out!

739
00:44:46,433 --> 00:44:47,768
It's not as simple as that.

740
00:44:47,851 --> 00:44:50,813
The Mitra got me all by myself,
and they were grilling me.

741
00:44:51,689 --> 00:44:53,607
I'm weak. I was scared.

742
00:44:54,525 --> 00:44:56,777
But I never thought
they'd try to execute her.

743
00:44:57,403 --> 00:44:58,278
But why?

744
00:44:58,362 --> 00:45:00,447
[both] What do you mean, execute her?

745
00:45:00,531 --> 00:45:03,409
I thought she'd be treated
just like all the other offenders.

746
00:45:03,492 --> 00:45:05,452
That she'd be thrown in a jail cell.

747
00:45:05,536 --> 00:45:06,370
[both] Huh?

748
00:45:06,453 --> 00:45:09,415
But then Lord Velvet drew his sword
and went for her.

749
00:45:09,998 --> 00:45:12,751
[sobbing] I'm so sorry. Please forgive me.

750
00:45:13,419 --> 00:45:17,214
Oh, come on, Chorogy.
Why are you the one crying now?

751
00:45:17,297 --> 00:45:18,924
I'll give you something to cry about.

752
00:45:19,007 --> 00:45:23,220
Hang on, Sapphire! I'll be there soon!
Zirco's coming to save you now!

753
00:45:23,303 --> 00:45:24,555
[Hecate] Are you really sorry?

754
00:45:24,638 --> 00:45:26,056
[Chorogy sobbing]

755
00:45:28,100 --> 00:45:29,560
-[Sapphire] Pine.
-[gasps]

756
00:45:31,437 --> 00:45:32,354
[Pine] Sapphire?

757
00:45:33,522 --> 00:45:36,483
-[chuckles] Sorry for making you worry.
-Sapphire!

758
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:38,610
Oh, thank goodness.

759
00:45:38,694 --> 00:45:42,030
[Zirco] Huh? Sa… Sapphire!
You're all right!

760
00:45:42,906 --> 00:45:44,074
-[Zirco sobbing]
-Huh?

761
00:45:44,158 --> 00:45:46,785
[gasps loudly] She's alive!

762
00:45:46,869 --> 00:45:49,079
I didn't mean to make you all worry.

763
00:45:49,705 --> 00:45:52,082
-[Pine] How did you get away?
-[Chorogy] Thank heavens.

764
00:45:52,166 --> 00:45:54,251
[Zirco] Don't tell me
you struck Velvet down!

765
00:45:54,960 --> 00:45:56,128
Of course not.

766
00:45:56,211 --> 00:45:57,838
I'm not sure how to say it.

767
00:45:57,921 --> 00:45:59,756
It's a bit of a long story.

768
00:46:02,134 --> 00:46:04,344
[electrical buzzing]

769
00:46:09,057 --> 00:46:10,934
Let go of me right now!

770
00:46:11,018 --> 00:46:13,395
I said, let me go!

771
00:46:13,479 --> 00:46:16,315
-Now you let go! [grunting]
-[Velvet] Why did you bring her along?

772
00:46:17,024 --> 00:46:19,318
Now that she knows,
she cannot leave here alive.

773
00:46:19,401 --> 00:46:21,737
No matter how many times
we turned her away,

774
00:46:21,820 --> 00:46:24,281
she kept following.
Shall I dispose of her?

775
00:46:24,990 --> 00:46:27,701
-No, wait!
-If you do anything to my Sapphire,

776
00:46:27,784 --> 00:46:29,870
I'll make sure you pay for it!

777
00:46:29,953 --> 00:46:31,955
She can be trusted. She's not a spy.

778
00:46:32,039 --> 00:46:33,457
[Velvet] Why should I believe that?

779
00:46:33,540 --> 00:46:36,752
What, do you get some kind of sick kick
out of bullying an old woman?

780
00:46:36,835 --> 00:46:39,796
[Velvet] Informants come in all shapes,
sizes and ages.

781
00:46:39,880 --> 00:46:42,466
{\an8}We've been together a long time.
She's family to me.

782
00:46:42,549 --> 00:46:45,344
[Zirco] I'll make you all pay!
I mean it! [grunts]

783
00:46:45,427 --> 00:46:47,804
-[Sapphire] I'm begging you.
-Let me go!

784
00:46:47,888 --> 00:46:48,889
[grunting]

785
00:46:49,431 --> 00:46:51,350
[scoffs] Very well, then.

786
00:46:51,433 --> 00:46:53,769
-[Zirco] Let go of me!
-She makes one suspicious move,

787
00:46:53,852 --> 00:46:55,521
she gets the sword.

788
00:46:56,230 --> 00:46:57,314
Now hurry up.

789
00:47:01,109 --> 00:47:04,363
<i>Where we are headed today</i>
<i>is the Pillar of Creation.</i>

790
00:47:05,656 --> 00:47:08,242
<i>They are gateways to the world</i>
<i>where the Nergal dwell.</i>

791
00:47:10,160 --> 00:47:12,704
<i>In truth, the Nergal</i>
<i>are not creatures of this world.</i>

792
00:47:14,081 --> 00:47:15,791
<i>They cannot be killed either.</i>

793
00:47:15,874 --> 00:47:17,584
<i>They may not even be alive at all.</i>

794
00:47:17,668 --> 00:47:19,962
[Sapphire] <i>These Nergal, what are they?</i>

795
00:47:20,462 --> 00:47:23,840
[Velvet] <i>All I know for sure is that</i>
<i>they are beings that devour souls.</i>

796
00:47:24,466 --> 00:47:27,052
<i>They can usually satiate</i>
<i>their hunger with crystals.</i>

797
00:47:27,678 --> 00:47:28,971
<i>But if the crystals run low,</i>

798
00:47:29,054 --> 00:47:31,807
<i>they come to the city</i>
<i>to devour human souls instead.</i>

799
00:47:31,890 --> 00:47:34,476
[Sapphire] <i>Can a creature like that</i>
<i>even be defeated?</i>

800
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:37,646
[Velvet] <i>The Nergal are connected</i>
<i>to our world by components called factors,</i>

801
00:47:37,729 --> 00:47:40,232
<i>and they could be destroyed.</i>
<i>Just one is not enough.</i>

802
00:47:40,774 --> 00:47:42,317
<i>But destroy all of them,</i>

803
00:47:42,401 --> 00:47:44,570
<i>and the King of Ash</i>
<i>could be severed from our world.</i>

804
00:47:45,279 --> 00:47:47,447
[Sapphire] <i>How can you say that</i>
<i>with such certainty?</i>

805
00:47:48,448 --> 00:47:51,410
[Velvet] <i>Look, at one time,</i>
<i>a great kingdom stood there.</i>

806
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:53,745
<i>No one alive remembers it now.</i>

807
00:47:54,371 --> 00:47:56,373
<i>But I discovered</i>
<i>some of their ancient records,</i>

808
00:47:56,456 --> 00:47:58,917
<i>and in them were accounts</i>
<i>of those who fought the Nergal.</i>

809
00:47:59,501 --> 00:48:02,212
[Sapphire] <i>Even so, their kingdom</i>
<i>was still destroyed.</i>

810
00:48:02,296 --> 00:48:04,590
[Velvet] <i>The Nergal that ravaged</i>
<i>this once great kingdom</i>

811
00:48:04,673 --> 00:48:07,175
<i>was most likely the same</i>
<i>that attacked your homeland.</i>

812
00:48:07,718 --> 00:48:08,552
[Sapphire] <i>What?</i>

813
00:48:09,094 --> 00:48:11,805
[Velvet] <i>It has appeared</i>
<i>at regular intervals throughout history,</i>

814
00:48:11,888 --> 00:48:13,765
<i>and caused the downfall of many a nation.</i>

815
00:48:14,516 --> 00:48:15,642
<i>The Prime Nergal.</i>

816
00:48:16,393 --> 00:48:19,021
[Sapphire] <i>So then,</i>
<i>I'll have to face that one, too?</i>

817
00:48:19,104 --> 00:48:22,190
[Velvet] <i>The Prime Nergal's return</i>
<i>is the cataclysm the Mitra feared most.</i>

818
00:48:22,983 --> 00:48:25,193
<i>Your powers might be</i>
<i>just what we need to understand</i>

819
00:48:25,277 --> 00:48:26,778
<i>the truth behind the King of Ash.</i>

820
00:48:28,238 --> 00:48:29,906
<i>And I intend to find out.</i>

821
00:48:32,367 --> 00:48:33,243
There it is.

822
00:48:35,162 --> 00:48:36,747
[Sapphire] That's a Pillar of Creation?

823
00:48:43,420 --> 00:48:45,255
[Velvet] The curse here is too strong.

824
00:48:45,339 --> 00:48:47,466
We can get no closer,
or risk being infected.

825
00:48:49,926 --> 00:48:50,844
What's the matter?

826
00:48:51,637 --> 00:48:53,597
Have you lost your nerve
now that you've seen it?

827
00:48:54,514 --> 00:48:56,391
Of course not. I'm ready.

828
00:48:57,351 --> 00:48:58,185
[Zirco] Ah!

829
00:48:58,852 --> 00:49:00,020
You're gonna want this.

830
00:49:00,103 --> 00:49:02,731
Wow. You finished it already?

831
00:49:02,814 --> 00:49:04,775
{\an8}Press here, and voila.

832
00:49:06,318 --> 00:49:07,527
{\an8}That should come in handy.

833
00:49:09,071 --> 00:49:10,614
{\an8}Thank you so much, Zirco.

834
00:49:12,240 --> 00:49:14,868
{\an8}Hmm. Just promise
you'll come back in one piece.

835
00:49:23,669 --> 00:49:26,088
[dramatic music playing]

836
00:49:43,021 --> 00:49:44,106
The gateway.

837
00:49:49,319 --> 00:49:50,195
Huh?

838
00:49:51,405 --> 00:49:52,280
Ah!

839
00:49:55,200 --> 00:49:58,078
[screaming]

840
00:50:04,710 --> 00:50:05,919
[grunts]

841
00:50:07,713 --> 00:50:10,173
The Princess Knight to the rescue.

842
00:50:13,719 --> 00:50:15,846
What is this place? Where am I?

843
00:50:17,514 --> 00:50:18,348
[gasps]

844
00:50:37,868 --> 00:50:41,413
[gasps] It can't be.
Is that Mother and Father?

845
00:50:45,917 --> 00:50:46,793
[groans]

846
00:50:47,753 --> 00:50:50,130
[groaning]

847
00:51:11,651 --> 00:51:13,904
The Nergal. They know I'm here.

848
00:51:21,953 --> 00:51:23,955
[roars]

849
00:51:30,170 --> 00:51:32,339
[roars]

850
00:51:43,892 --> 00:51:45,101
{\an8}I haven't seen this.

851
00:51:46,520 --> 00:51:48,897
[Sapphire screaming]

852
00:51:57,739 --> 00:51:59,282
This thing is amazing.

853
00:52:02,828 --> 00:52:03,954
Just four left.

854
00:52:05,914 --> 00:52:06,957
Let's go.

855
00:52:08,667 --> 00:52:10,043
[grunting]

856
00:52:32,983 --> 00:52:34,609
That worked.

857
00:52:42,993 --> 00:52:43,952
[effort scream]

858
00:52:52,627 --> 00:52:53,503
[Queen] <i>Sapphire.</i>

859
00:52:54,254 --> 00:52:55,839
You must not resist.

860
00:52:55,922 --> 00:52:58,758
Don't fight,
even if the whole world should perish.

861
00:52:59,593 --> 00:53:01,970
[majestic music playing]

862
00:53:40,967 --> 00:53:43,178
[rumbling]

863
00:53:44,054 --> 00:53:44,971
What's going on?

864
00:53:45,931 --> 00:53:47,057
[whooshes]

865
00:54:00,820 --> 00:54:04,199
All I have to do is destroy that?
All right.

866
00:54:08,954 --> 00:54:12,040
[grunting, straining]

867
00:54:24,052 --> 00:54:25,136
Did it work?

868
00:54:25,220 --> 00:54:28,974
[whooshing]

869
00:54:30,183 --> 00:54:31,142
[creaking]

870
00:54:31,226 --> 00:54:32,936
-[whooshing]
-[Sapphire exclaims loudly]

871
00:54:36,564 --> 00:54:37,524
[grunting]

872
00:54:39,192 --> 00:54:42,070
Huh? What's all this now?

873
00:54:42,153 --> 00:54:43,780
[tinkling melodically]

874
00:54:46,616 --> 00:54:48,827
[yelling fearfully]

875
00:54:48,910 --> 00:54:50,870
I'm in trouble! I'm in trouble!

876
00:54:53,206 --> 00:54:54,374
[grunting]

877
00:55:01,756 --> 00:55:03,341
[panting] It's falling!

878
00:55:04,300 --> 00:55:05,885
[screaming]

879
00:55:08,304 --> 00:55:09,723
[continues screaming]

880
00:55:17,105 --> 00:55:18,982
[crackling]

881
00:55:19,941 --> 00:55:21,943
Sapphire is still inside!

882
00:55:23,361 --> 00:55:24,404
[exhales heavily]

883
00:55:24,487 --> 00:55:25,780
[rumbling]

884
00:55:25,864 --> 00:55:27,115
[wind howling]

885
00:55:29,451 --> 00:55:31,536
[footsteps approaching]

886
00:55:34,456 --> 00:55:36,041
[snickers softly]

887
00:55:39,335 --> 00:55:41,296
[electrical buzzing]

888
00:55:44,049 --> 00:55:45,508
-[jingles]
-[Sapphire] What's this?

889
00:55:45,592 --> 00:55:47,177
-[coins jingle]
-[Sapphire, Zirco gasp]

890
00:55:47,260 --> 00:55:48,636
It's your payment.

891
00:55:48,720 --> 00:55:51,347
You never said the job came with payment!

892
00:55:51,431 --> 00:55:54,309
Hmm. Why would you think it wouldn't?

893
00:55:54,976 --> 00:55:56,978
Oh. [laughs exultantly]

894
00:55:57,062 --> 00:55:58,980
[upbeat music playing]

895
00:55:59,064 --> 00:56:00,940
[Zirco] Hmm.

896
00:56:01,024 --> 00:56:02,358
[Zirco laughs gleefully]

897
00:56:02,984 --> 00:56:07,739
Ah! There's no restaurant in town
that'll turn us away now!

898
00:56:07,822 --> 00:56:09,866
-[Zirco giggling]
-[Sapphire chuckles]

899
00:56:09,949 --> 00:56:12,327
[male server]
Roasted golden rat with herb sauce.

900
00:56:12,410 --> 00:56:14,287
-[Sapphire and Zirco exclaim]
-Please enjoy.

901
00:56:14,370 --> 00:56:15,705
[Sapphire and Zirco laughing]

902
00:56:15,789 --> 00:56:17,749
[Sapphire and Zirco]
And without further ado…

903
00:56:17,832 --> 00:56:19,626
[both gobble greedily]

904
00:56:21,878 --> 00:56:25,090
[Pine] <i>♪ In a foreign tongue ♪</i>

905
00:56:25,173 --> 00:56:28,426
♪ <i>From a distant land </i>♪

906
00:56:28,510 --> 00:56:33,098
<i>♪ You offered the same prayer</i>
<i>Again and again ♪</i>

907
00:56:35,600 --> 00:56:36,976
-I'm sorry.
-Huh?

908
00:56:37,060 --> 00:56:40,438
I'm sure you had better things to do
than this on your day off.

909
00:56:40,522 --> 00:56:42,273
What are you talking about, Pine?

910
00:56:42,357 --> 00:56:44,484
This is just the kind of break I needed.

911
00:56:44,567 --> 00:56:47,654
After all, Velvet's been working me
to the bone lately.

912
00:56:48,947 --> 00:56:53,409
I think I've finally found it,
the reason that I survived.

913
00:56:54,327 --> 00:56:55,829
Enough about me.

914
00:56:55,912 --> 00:56:58,164
I want to hear more about
what you can do, Pine.

915
00:56:58,748 --> 00:57:01,167
{\an8}Sapphire! Don't push yourself too hard.

916
00:57:01,251 --> 00:57:02,627
-[Hakobe] Wow!
-[gasps]

917
00:57:03,336 --> 00:57:04,587
She's got a flute!

918
00:57:04,671 --> 00:57:06,131
I told you to wait.

919
00:57:07,465 --> 00:57:09,300
Stop, Hakobe.

920
00:57:09,384 --> 00:57:10,802
Don't bother other people.

921
00:57:10,885 --> 00:57:13,221
{\an8}I'm not bothering anyone.

922
00:57:13,304 --> 00:57:15,974
-[Nazuna] I guess you're just a kid.
-[gasps] Velvet?

923
00:57:16,057 --> 00:57:18,685
[Nazuna] Why do you always have
to be like this, Hakobe?

924
00:57:18,768 --> 00:57:20,687
You've got your bad habits too, Nazuna.

925
00:57:20,770 --> 00:57:22,522
Why don't you join us?

926
00:57:26,860 --> 00:57:28,069
Do you know this song?

927
00:57:28,695 --> 00:57:29,696
Yeah.

928
00:57:30,613 --> 00:57:33,116
it's "The Winter-Worn Traveler", right?

929
00:57:33,199 --> 00:57:35,201
Would you play it again?

930
00:57:35,285 --> 00:57:36,744
You must like music.

931
00:57:36,828 --> 00:57:37,912
Yeah.

932
00:57:38,663 --> 00:57:41,332
We're always singing
and learning new songs together.

933
00:57:42,250 --> 00:57:45,420
Well, this is Pine,
and she's a really good singer, too.

934
00:57:45,503 --> 00:57:47,547
-Shall we have a listen?
-Wait! Sapphire!

935
00:57:47,630 --> 00:57:49,507
[both gasping]

936
00:57:49,591 --> 00:57:51,968
-[flute playing]
-[Pine inhales]

937
00:57:52,051 --> 00:57:55,472
<i>♪ Long, long ago ♪</i>

938
00:57:55,555 --> 00:57:58,266
<i>♪ A lone girl… ♪</i>

939
00:57:58,349 --> 00:57:59,976
<i>-♪ Wandered the land… ♪</i>
-[Sapphire] Huh?

940
00:58:00,059 --> 00:58:01,186
[Pine struggles to sing]

941
00:58:01,269 --> 00:58:03,146
[boys snickering]

942
00:58:03,229 --> 00:58:05,231
[groans helplessly]

943
00:58:07,692 --> 00:58:08,985
-[pops]
-Whoa!

944
00:58:09,068 --> 00:58:11,279
Pine! Are you all right?

945
00:58:11,362 --> 00:58:12,739
[Pine groaning]

946
00:58:16,451 --> 00:58:17,702
[Pine groans softly]

947
00:58:23,750 --> 00:58:25,126
[gasping]

948
00:58:25,877 --> 00:58:27,420
[whimpers]

949
00:58:27,504 --> 00:58:28,546
[sighs]

950
00:58:29,797 --> 00:58:31,925
-Sorry for interrupting.
-[gasps]

951
00:58:33,301 --> 00:58:35,011
Well…

952
00:58:35,094 --> 00:58:36,930
No, not at all.

953
00:58:37,013 --> 00:58:38,348
Don't worry about it.

954
00:58:41,476 --> 00:58:44,312
Um, do you know those children?

955
00:58:44,395 --> 00:58:46,272
[Velvet] They're my siblings.

956
00:58:46,356 --> 00:58:47,857
This is where I was raised.

957
00:58:48,816 --> 00:58:51,319
[kids] <i>♪ O King… ♪</i>

958
00:58:51,402 --> 00:58:52,403
Is something wrong?

959
00:58:54,697 --> 00:58:57,909
It's just, Sapphire's been
coming home exhausted every day.

960
00:58:59,285 --> 00:59:00,954
What are you making her do?

961
00:59:01,496 --> 00:59:04,207
I'm giving her a chance to atone.

962
00:59:04,290 --> 00:59:05,792
Atone for what?

963
00:59:05,875 --> 00:59:07,335
She hasn't told you?

964
00:59:07,418 --> 00:59:08,962
Maybe you should ask her yourself.

965
00:59:09,045 --> 00:59:14,342
[kids] <i>♪ A blue bud ♪</i>

966
00:59:14,425 --> 00:59:16,302
[Pine] I know this song.

967
00:59:16,386 --> 00:59:21,599
<i>♪ A pure angel given in sacrifice ♪</i>

968
00:59:21,683 --> 00:59:23,601
I won't let them be sacrificed.

969
00:59:25,478 --> 00:59:27,355
-[wind blowing]
-[grass rustling]

970
00:59:28,439 --> 00:59:30,525
[squeaking]

971
00:59:32,402 --> 00:59:33,778
[explosion booms]

972
00:59:41,286 --> 00:59:42,870
[solemn music playing]

973
00:59:49,669 --> 00:59:51,087
[men exclaiming]

974
00:59:52,005 --> 00:59:53,715
[White Mitra] No, not here!

975
00:59:56,676 --> 00:59:58,595
[Velvet]
The last confirmed sighting of a Nergal

976
00:59:58,678 --> 01:00:00,638
was over three months ago.

977
01:00:01,472 --> 01:00:04,267
The mining sites seem
to be recovering well.

978
01:00:04,350 --> 01:00:06,728
In fact, our output
has not only rebounded,

979
01:00:06,811 --> 01:00:09,480
but has significantly increased.

980
01:00:09,564 --> 01:00:10,815
Excellent.

981
01:00:10,898 --> 01:00:15,612
[Mitra] Moving on, we have more
information regarding the recent fire.

982
01:00:17,405 --> 01:00:19,741
[White Mitra] Excuse the intrusion,
but there is something

983
01:00:19,824 --> 01:00:22,785
that I must urgently bring
to Your Holiness' attention.

984
01:00:27,749 --> 01:00:30,543
And you have no idea
as to what might have caused this?

985
01:00:30,627 --> 01:00:32,337
[Velvet] I do not. None at all.

986
01:00:32,420 --> 01:00:35,923
For now, our sterilization team
can keep things under control.

987
01:00:36,007 --> 01:00:38,009
Should the situation get any worse,

988
01:00:38,092 --> 01:00:40,428
we'll need to resort
to emergency provisions.

989
01:00:40,511 --> 01:00:44,307
We should prepare the sacrificial rites,
should the need present itself.

990
01:00:45,558 --> 01:00:47,644
[Velvet] Understood, Your Holiness

991
01:00:48,394 --> 01:00:51,397
Velvet, after all we've done to raise you,

992
01:00:51,481 --> 01:00:54,609
I trust I don't need to stress
that betrayal would be unforgivable.

993
01:00:54,692 --> 01:00:56,861
You have nothing to fear.

994
01:00:56,944 --> 01:00:59,864
I assure you, I will not disappoint you.

995
01:01:02,158 --> 01:01:03,493
[footsteps approaching]

996
01:01:03,576 --> 01:01:04,994
[door opens]

997
01:01:05,953 --> 01:01:08,831
You called, so here I am.

998
01:01:10,166 --> 01:01:12,168
[grunts softly]

999
01:01:12,251 --> 01:01:14,420
What is it? What do you need?

1000
01:01:14,504 --> 01:01:16,839
Why make me sneak all the way in here?

1001
01:01:16,923 --> 01:01:18,549
[Velvet] We have to pause our mission.

1002
01:01:18,633 --> 01:01:21,969
We can't make any further attempts
to take down the Pillars or the Nergal.

1003
01:01:22,053 --> 01:01:23,638
[Sapphire] Huh? Why not?

1004
01:01:24,472 --> 01:01:27,558
The pillars of creation
have begun appearing at the city gate.

1005
01:01:28,518 --> 01:01:31,270
[Velvet] We must be cautious
not to provoke the King of Ash further.

1006
01:01:31,354 --> 01:01:32,772
[Sapphire] We have to do something.

1007
01:01:32,855 --> 01:01:34,482
We can't just let them grow.

1008
01:01:34,565 --> 01:01:36,526
[Velvet] The Mitra have their methods.

1009
01:01:36,609 --> 01:01:38,569
We'll just wait for things to settle down.

1010
01:01:38,653 --> 01:01:41,030
[Sapphire] Wouldn't it be faster
if I took care of it?

1011
01:01:41,114 --> 01:01:43,491
I'm not just gonna sit there and watch.

1012
01:01:44,367 --> 01:01:46,327
The Mitra are not so incompetent.

1013
01:01:46,411 --> 01:01:48,830
An infestation of this scale
can be handled.

1014
01:01:48,913 --> 01:01:51,499
The immigrant district
is right next to the gate.

1015
01:01:52,333 --> 01:01:54,001
If the growth gets out of hand…

1016
01:01:55,378 --> 01:01:57,547
more than one person
might become a victim.

1017
01:01:58,589 --> 01:01:59,799
[Velvet scoffs]

1018
01:01:59,882 --> 01:02:03,177
How do you expect to save the world
without sacrifice?

1019
01:02:03,261 --> 01:02:06,514
That's how you were saved…
by the sacrifice of your kingdom.

1020
01:02:07,557 --> 01:02:10,143
{\an8}Hmm. That's why I want to change things.

1021
01:02:10,852 --> 01:02:14,021
{\an8}If I know danger is approaching,
I can't ignore it.

1022
01:02:14,564 --> 01:02:16,733
{\an8}I don't want to lose anyone else.

1023
01:02:17,942 --> 01:02:21,320
{\an8}Do you think you're truly
capable of containing it?

1024
01:02:21,404 --> 01:02:24,824
{\an8}If the Pillars of Creation
can't be stopped and keep growing,

1025
01:02:24,907 --> 01:02:27,702
{\an8}and one of the Nergal appears once more,

1026
01:02:27,785 --> 01:02:31,330
{\an8}the Mitra will have no choice
but to demand a sacrifice.

1027
01:02:31,414 --> 01:02:33,124
{\an8}What are you talking about?

1028
01:02:33,207 --> 01:02:34,959
{\an8}The sacrifices offered here

1029
01:02:35,042 --> 01:02:36,544
are the church's orphans.

1030
01:02:36,627 --> 01:02:38,045
[gasps]

1031
01:02:38,129 --> 01:02:40,006
They're like you, Sapphire,

1032
01:02:40,089 --> 01:02:41,758
doomed to a cursed fate.

1033
01:02:43,801 --> 01:02:45,344
I understand.

1034
01:02:45,428 --> 01:02:46,721
You want to save them.

1035
01:02:46,804 --> 01:02:47,889
Velvet, I can help.

1036
01:02:47,972 --> 01:02:51,559
How dare you presume to understand
someone else's heart?

1037
01:02:52,518 --> 01:02:57,231
Your little imagined reality
is not the same as my truth.

1038
01:02:57,982 --> 01:02:59,150
[exhales]

1039
01:03:00,443 --> 01:03:01,736
I'll do it.

1040
01:03:01,819 --> 01:03:03,321
I'll be the sacrifice.

1041
01:03:04,155 --> 01:03:07,408
After all, it was meant to be
my destiny in Silverland.

1042
01:03:08,201 --> 01:03:09,869
So if I can't stop it first,

1043
01:03:09,952 --> 01:03:11,537
I'll take their place.

1044
01:03:12,997 --> 01:03:14,582
Please.

1045
01:03:14,665 --> 01:03:16,542
Let me keep fighting till the end.

1046
01:03:18,836 --> 01:03:20,922
Don't let my power go to waste.

1047
01:03:24,842 --> 01:03:26,719
[electrical buzzing]

1048
01:03:29,972 --> 01:03:32,058
[White Mitra 1]
This area is currently sealed off.

1049
01:03:32,141 --> 01:03:35,144
-[man] You really have it under control?
-[White Mitra 2] Don't push.

1050
01:03:35,228 --> 01:03:36,646
Please, for your own safety.

1051
01:03:36,729 --> 01:03:40,149
We are asking all citizens
to remain inside their homes.

1052
01:03:42,026 --> 01:03:43,986
[White Mitra 3]
It seems to be contained for now.

1053
01:03:44,070 --> 01:03:46,989
[White Mitra 4] The pillar respawn rate
is also decreasing.

1054
01:03:49,617 --> 01:03:51,786
[White Mitra 5]
That very nearly took us to the brink,

1055
01:03:51,869 --> 01:03:53,037
but we're stopping it.

1056
01:03:53,120 --> 01:03:54,288
[people clamoring]

1057
01:03:56,916 --> 01:03:58,084
[clamor continues]

1058
01:03:58,167 --> 01:03:59,669
[Sapphire] Everyone, remain calm!

1059
01:03:59,752 --> 01:04:00,837
[dramatic music playing]

1060
01:04:00,920 --> 01:04:02,213
[people exclaiming]

1061
01:04:04,090 --> 01:04:06,175
The Princess Knight to the rescue!

1062
01:04:06,259 --> 01:04:07,385
-Oh!
-Oh!

1063
01:04:07,468 --> 01:04:08,845
It's the Princess Knight!

1064
01:04:10,888 --> 01:04:12,765
You don't need to worry.

1065
01:04:12,849 --> 01:04:14,350
[woman] Thank goodness!

1066
01:04:14,433 --> 01:04:15,726
[man] She'll save us!

1067
01:04:15,810 --> 01:04:17,103
[fire roaring]

1068
01:04:18,187 --> 01:04:19,689
[music continues]

1069
01:04:19,772 --> 01:04:21,649
[bleating]

1070
01:04:21,732 --> 01:04:22,733
[gasping]

1071
01:04:23,442 --> 01:04:24,652
[bubbling]

1072
01:04:25,361 --> 01:04:26,362
[explosion]

1073
01:04:26,445 --> 01:04:27,655
[people screaming]

1074
01:04:28,364 --> 01:04:30,116
[man] The tower is collapsing!

1075
01:04:32,285 --> 01:04:33,578
No way!

1076
01:04:42,920 --> 01:04:46,757
No, no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no you don't!

1077
01:04:46,841 --> 01:04:48,259
That thing is huge.

1078
01:04:48,342 --> 01:04:50,011
Is she gonna be able to stop it?

1079
01:04:51,429 --> 01:04:52,930
[grunts]

1080
01:04:53,014 --> 01:04:54,098
[Pine panting]

1081
01:04:55,099 --> 01:04:56,601
[Zirco] Whoa!

1082
01:04:56,684 --> 01:04:58,269
What's going on?

1083
01:04:58,853 --> 01:04:59,896
[barking]

1084
01:05:01,522 --> 01:05:03,774
[Mitra 1] An evacuation order
has been issued.

1085
01:05:03,858 --> 01:05:05,318
All citizens must comply.

1086
01:05:05,401 --> 01:05:07,653
-Come, darling, this way.
-[Mitra 1] Women and children…

1087
01:05:07,737 --> 01:05:09,238
Can you tell us what's happening?

1088
01:05:09,322 --> 01:05:10,656
[sobbing]

1089
01:05:10,740 --> 01:05:14,327
[Mitra 2] It's going to be all right.
Do you know where your parents are?

1090
01:05:14,410 --> 01:05:15,870
[gate bangs loudly]

1091
01:05:15,953 --> 01:05:17,580
[guard 1] Move back! Move back!

1092
01:05:17,663 --> 01:05:19,165
[man] Wait! You can't do this.

1093
01:05:20,708 --> 01:05:23,377
[guard 2]
Full domestic lockdown is now in effect.

1094
01:05:23,461 --> 01:05:25,379
[people clamoring]

1095
01:05:26,839 --> 01:05:28,382
[bell clanging continuously]

1096
01:05:35,932 --> 01:05:37,767
-[Mitra] Found it.
-[White Mitra] Well done.

1097
01:05:37,850 --> 01:05:40,186
[bell continues clanging]

1098
01:05:44,023 --> 01:05:47,068
[Velvet] Pardon the intrusion,
Your Holiness.

1099
01:05:47,151 --> 01:05:48,819
-[cutlery clinks]
-[Pope] You may enter.

1100
01:05:53,240 --> 01:05:55,618
You summoned me, so I have dutifully come.

1101
01:05:59,956 --> 01:06:02,458
I suspect that you already know why.

1102
01:06:03,042 --> 01:06:04,460
[clanging]

1103
01:06:04,543 --> 01:06:06,837
[suspenseful music playing]

1104
01:06:07,463 --> 01:06:09,548
This is your doing, isn't it?

1105
01:06:13,552 --> 01:06:14,804
Yes.

1106
01:06:15,429 --> 01:06:16,430
[sighs wearily]

1107
01:06:16,514 --> 01:06:19,976
But Your Holiness,
I believe that girl may very well be

1108
01:06:20,059 --> 01:06:22,395
the Angel of Hope
that we have so long awaited.

1109
01:06:23,396 --> 01:06:27,149
With her mysterious powers, she was able
to successfully seal away a Nergal.

1110
01:06:27,817 --> 01:06:29,652
And not just once or twice.

1111
01:06:29,735 --> 01:06:32,738
I understand that toppling a Nergal
goes against the Mitra customs,

1112
01:06:32,822 --> 01:06:35,950
but the power she possesses
could potentially put an end

1113
01:06:36,033 --> 01:06:38,077
to all of our suffering, once and for all.

1114
01:06:38,160 --> 01:06:39,912
Velvet. Listen.

1115
01:06:39,996 --> 01:06:41,205
Yes, sir.

1116
01:06:41,288 --> 01:06:45,418
That immigrant girl,
she is not our Angel of Hope.

1117
01:06:45,501 --> 01:06:46,627
But Your Holiness--

1118
01:06:46,711 --> 01:06:49,714
You place far too much faith
in human beings.

1119
01:06:49,797 --> 01:06:51,257
[Velvet gasps]

1120
01:06:51,340 --> 01:06:55,886
We humans are not nearly as strong
as you hope and believe us to be.

1121
01:06:55,970 --> 01:07:00,141
It is an inescapable truth for all people,
including that girl.

1122
01:07:00,224 --> 01:07:02,977
And being the weak
and frail beings that they are,

1123
01:07:03,060 --> 01:07:06,564
when they are subjected
to cruel trials, they break.

1124
01:07:06,647 --> 01:07:10,860
That is why we, the Mitra,
must help guide and govern the hapless

1125
01:07:10,943 --> 01:07:13,696
and, at times, serve as a shield as well.

1126
01:07:13,779 --> 01:07:15,197
There must be another way.

1127
01:07:16,115 --> 01:07:17,992
Do not forget your teachings, Velvet.

1128
01:07:18,075 --> 01:07:20,953
Human beings are weak of heart and spirit.

1129
01:07:21,037 --> 01:07:24,290
Only by finding a common enemy
can they truly work together

1130
01:07:24,373 --> 01:07:26,250
for the progress of their kind.

1131
01:07:26,333 --> 01:07:29,879
This applies to you…
and yes, even to myself.

1132
01:07:29,962 --> 01:07:31,047
Your Holiness.

1133
01:07:32,214 --> 01:07:33,215
I can't just…

1134
01:07:33,299 --> 01:07:34,884
I have to do something.

1135
01:07:36,093 --> 01:07:39,930
{\an8}The weak and frail creatures of this world
are sacrificed to power.

1136
01:07:40,014 --> 01:07:42,475
{\an8}A law as constant as the sun.

1137
01:07:42,558 --> 01:07:46,437
{\an8}Humankind is mercilessly
assailed by the King of Ash.

1138
01:07:46,520 --> 01:07:49,982
{\an8}That is the unalterable
natural state of our existence.

1139
01:07:50,900 --> 01:07:54,320
Just as humans gain their sustenance
from Golden Rats,

1140
01:07:54,403 --> 01:07:58,074
humans, then, must serve
as nourishment for the king.

1141
01:07:58,157 --> 01:08:01,077
{\an8}Humanity is happiest
when it is kept safe and cloistered,

1142
01:08:01,160 --> 01:08:03,412
{\an8}where the illusion of peace eases them.

1143
01:08:04,497 --> 01:08:06,791
{\an8}But you and the girl
have shattered that dream.

1144
01:08:07,500 --> 01:08:08,751
[Velvet breathes shakily]

1145
01:08:11,253 --> 01:08:13,089
[pensive music playing]

1146
01:08:21,889 --> 01:08:24,475
-[guard 1] Report the situation.
-[guard 2] Yes, sir.

1147
01:08:24,558 --> 01:08:28,521
It appears there is someone
fighting a Nergal at the city gate.

1148
01:08:28,604 --> 01:08:31,148
[guard 1 exhales] Let's move out!

1149
01:08:31,232 --> 01:08:32,566
[guard 2] Yes, sir.

1150
01:08:32,650 --> 01:08:34,360
[both panting]

1151
01:08:34,443 --> 01:08:36,070
[all gasping]

1152
01:08:36,695 --> 01:08:37,988
That can't be good.

1153
01:08:39,615 --> 01:08:40,658
Sapphire!

1154
01:08:40,741 --> 01:08:42,660
-[Chorogy] Time to take a stand!
-[all] Huh?

1155
01:08:43,410 --> 01:08:44,620
[snickers]

1156
01:08:45,246 --> 01:08:47,039
[Pine] Ch… Chorogy?

1157
01:08:47,123 --> 01:08:49,500
What the hell are you wearing?

1158
01:08:50,835 --> 01:08:52,044
Are you just gonna sit around

1159
01:08:52,128 --> 01:08:54,130
when we could be helping
the Princess Knight?

1160
01:08:55,047 --> 01:08:56,465
[Rock] Help her? How?

1161
01:08:57,049 --> 01:08:59,343
How are you gonna fight a Nergal?

1162
01:08:59,426 --> 01:09:00,469
What are you thinking?

1163
01:09:00,553 --> 01:09:01,887
[Chick and Tack] There's no way!

1164
01:09:01,971 --> 01:09:03,430
[Zirco] You could be killed!

1165
01:09:04,140 --> 01:09:06,725
I'm not sure how,
but even if we can't fight that thing,

1166
01:09:06,809 --> 01:09:08,686
there must be something we can do.

1167
01:09:08,769 --> 01:09:10,896
I've got things I want to protect, too.

1168
01:09:11,897 --> 01:09:14,150
If we want to help,
we gotta do it ourselves.

1169
01:09:15,734 --> 01:09:17,027
You're right, Chorogy.

1170
01:09:17,111 --> 01:09:18,821
You can count me in.

1171
01:09:18,904 --> 01:09:20,906
I'm always just the one getting saved.

1172
01:09:21,907 --> 01:09:23,617
It's about time I return the favor.

1173
01:09:23,701 --> 01:09:25,744
[gasps] I'll go, too!

1174
01:09:26,453 --> 01:09:29,165
[Chick] You're right. Let's do this.

1175
01:09:29,248 --> 01:09:31,792
[Tack] If Chorogy can find
the courage then…

1176
01:09:31,876 --> 01:09:33,794
[Zirco] I guess that leaves me no choice.

1177
01:09:33,878 --> 01:09:35,171
The old lady is in, too.

1178
01:09:35,254 --> 01:09:37,089
-[Chick and Tack] Yay!
-[Zirco] Let's do this.

1179
01:09:37,173 --> 01:09:38,591
[Rock] Sapphire needs us!

1180
01:09:40,092 --> 01:09:41,343
[clanging]

1181
01:09:43,053 --> 01:09:44,180
[clanging]

1182
01:09:45,347 --> 01:09:46,640
[crackling]

1183
01:09:49,018 --> 01:09:50,769
[panting]

1184
01:09:50,853 --> 01:09:51,854
It's no use.

1185
01:09:51,937 --> 01:09:53,063
They just keep coming.

1186
01:09:53,147 --> 01:09:55,149
[guard 1] What do you think you're doing?

1187
01:09:55,232 --> 01:09:56,233
[grunting]

1188
01:09:56,317 --> 01:09:58,611
Get your hands off!

1189
01:09:58,694 --> 01:09:59,528
[loud clanging]

1190
01:10:00,654 --> 01:10:02,156
[rumbling]

1191
01:10:02,656 --> 01:10:04,200
[all grunting]

1192
01:10:04,283 --> 01:10:05,451
Hmm?

1193
01:10:07,703 --> 01:10:09,079
Whoa!

1194
01:10:09,163 --> 01:10:10,789
[ominous music playing]

1195
01:10:16,545 --> 01:10:18,172
[Sapphire grunting, straining]

1196
01:10:18,714 --> 01:10:21,008
[effort scream]

1197
01:10:21,091 --> 01:10:22,885
[ominous music continues]

1198
01:10:40,694 --> 01:10:42,321
[lightning crashing]

1199
01:10:42,404 --> 01:10:45,491
[melancholy music playing]

1200
01:10:45,574 --> 01:10:47,534
[girl sobbing]

1201
01:10:47,618 --> 01:10:49,536
[woman sobbing]

1202
01:10:55,042 --> 01:10:56,919
[explosion]

1203
01:10:59,171 --> 01:11:00,547
[rumbling]

1204
01:11:03,259 --> 01:11:04,635
[whimpering]

1205
01:11:08,931 --> 01:11:10,849
What? What's going on?

1206
01:11:10,933 --> 01:11:12,101
[gasps]

1207
01:11:15,604 --> 01:11:16,855
[explosion]

1208
01:11:19,358 --> 01:11:21,277
[melancholy music continues]

1209
01:11:26,073 --> 01:11:28,450
[screeching]

1210
01:11:31,078 --> 01:11:32,705
[exhales]

1211
01:11:35,874 --> 01:11:37,751
The Prime Nergal.

1212
01:11:52,057 --> 01:11:53,600
What in the world happened?

1213
01:11:53,684 --> 01:11:55,144
What the hell is this?

1214
01:11:55,227 --> 01:11:57,021
[Hecate] This can't be real.

1215
01:11:57,104 --> 01:11:59,815
[gasps] How did this happen?

1216
01:11:59,898 --> 01:12:01,108
[Zirco] Oh.

1217
01:12:01,191 --> 01:12:02,234
[screeches]

1218
01:12:06,655 --> 01:12:07,865
[low growl]

1219
01:12:08,657 --> 01:12:09,825
[screeches]

1220
01:12:11,285 --> 01:12:12,953
[people clamoring, screaming]

1221
01:12:14,663 --> 01:12:16,081
I have to help!

1222
01:12:16,165 --> 01:12:17,207
Wait, Chorogy!

1223
01:12:35,267 --> 01:12:36,769
[tense music playing]

1224
01:12:39,563 --> 01:12:42,441
[people clamor in alarm]

1225
01:12:42,524 --> 01:12:44,735
[man] It's opening! It's open!

1226
01:12:50,449 --> 01:12:51,492
[squawks]

1227
01:12:57,206 --> 01:12:58,957
[metallic clanging]

1228
01:12:59,041 --> 01:13:00,084
[Sapphire grunts]

1229
01:13:00,167 --> 01:13:02,127
[screams echo]

1230
01:13:05,756 --> 01:13:07,341
[Sapphire straining]

1231
01:13:14,014 --> 01:13:15,265
[effort scream]

1232
01:13:15,849 --> 01:13:17,434
[screeching]

1233
01:13:18,894 --> 01:13:20,687
[Rock grunting]

1234
01:13:20,771 --> 01:13:22,439
The timing couldn't be worse.

1235
01:13:22,523 --> 01:13:24,650
Don't worry. I think it's just a sprain.

1236
01:13:25,734 --> 01:13:27,236
Wait, where's Chorogy?

1237
01:13:27,319 --> 01:13:28,862
He ran off up ahead.

1238
01:13:29,655 --> 01:13:31,156
[people whimper distantly]

1239
01:13:32,574 --> 01:13:33,784
[cracking]

1240
01:13:34,451 --> 01:13:35,953
[girl screaming]

1241
01:13:36,036 --> 01:13:38,247
Watch out! [grunts]

1242
01:13:38,330 --> 01:13:39,331
[thudding]

1243
01:13:40,666 --> 01:13:42,709
[Chorogy panting]

1244
01:13:42,793 --> 01:13:44,253
[whimpers]

1245
01:13:46,630 --> 01:13:47,714
[Chorogy chuckles]

1246
01:13:47,798 --> 01:13:50,050
-You're all right now.
-Mm-hmm.

1247
01:13:50,134 --> 01:13:52,177
[woman] Oh! Thank you so much.

1248
01:13:52,719 --> 01:13:54,471
-Oh!
-Thanks, mister.

1249
01:13:56,682 --> 01:13:59,768
I may not be able to fight,
but I can help people.

1250
01:13:59,852 --> 01:14:02,104
[distant groaning, howling]

1251
01:14:04,523 --> 01:14:05,691
Huh?

1252
01:14:07,359 --> 01:14:08,527
[gasps]

1253
01:14:09,319 --> 01:14:10,571
You're kidding.

1254
01:14:13,866 --> 01:14:15,242
[explosion]

1255
01:14:18,245 --> 01:14:20,747
[Nergal shrieks]

1256
01:14:23,834 --> 01:14:25,752
[all gasping]

1257
01:14:25,836 --> 01:14:28,088
Wait, was that…

1258
01:14:28,797 --> 01:14:31,800
[screaming] Chorogy!

1259
01:14:31,884 --> 01:14:34,511
[dramatic music playing]

1260
01:14:46,607 --> 01:14:48,442
[breathing shakily]

1261
01:14:49,193 --> 01:14:51,528
You can do it, Sapphire!

1262
01:14:53,906 --> 01:14:57,451
{\an8}Please, Sapphire! Take out that Nergal!

1263
01:14:58,035 --> 01:14:59,286
-Take it down!
-Take it down!

1264
01:14:59,369 --> 01:15:00,996
We're counting on you, Sapphire!

1265
01:15:01,079 --> 01:15:02,956
[dramatic music continues]

1266
01:15:05,250 --> 01:15:06,585
[man 1] Someone's fighting it.

1267
01:15:06,668 --> 01:15:08,253
[man 2] Is someone trying to stop it?

1268
01:15:08,337 --> 01:15:10,130
[woman] Is it the Angel of Hope?

1269
01:15:10,214 --> 01:15:11,965
It doesn't matter who it is.

1270
01:15:12,049 --> 01:15:14,718
We're begging you. Please, save us!

1271
01:15:14,801 --> 01:15:16,303
[dramatic music continues]

1272
01:15:19,223 --> 01:15:21,600
[Sapphire grunting, straining]

1273
01:15:23,894 --> 01:15:25,687
[grunting]

1274
01:15:32,361 --> 01:15:33,612
[man 1] What is that?

1275
01:15:34,988 --> 01:15:36,406
[woman] It's the Angel!

1276
01:15:37,074 --> 01:15:38,158
Angel of Hope,

1277
01:15:38,784 --> 01:15:39,868
please save us.

1278
01:15:39,952 --> 01:15:41,453
[sword clanking]

1279
01:15:50,045 --> 01:15:51,088
[grunts]

1280
01:15:52,506 --> 01:15:54,091
[music intensifies]

1281
01:15:54,174 --> 01:15:55,384
[sword clanking]

1282
01:15:59,763 --> 01:16:01,056
[effort scream]

1283
01:16:06,770 --> 01:16:08,105
[fearful panting]

1284
01:16:30,961 --> 01:16:32,212
[music fades]

1285
01:16:32,296 --> 01:16:34,131
[low rumbling]

1286
01:16:46,977 --> 01:16:50,897
[roaring]

1287
01:16:51,732 --> 01:16:52,858
[gasps] Hmm.

1288
01:16:54,901 --> 01:16:56,570
[explosion]

1289
01:16:58,071 --> 01:16:59,656
[breathing shakily]

1290
01:17:06,955 --> 01:17:08,332
[loud splash]

1291
01:17:13,462 --> 01:17:15,047
[clinking]

1292
01:17:16,423 --> 01:17:18,550
[rain pattering]

1293
01:17:25,432 --> 01:17:27,100
It's still here?

1294
01:17:27,184 --> 01:17:29,102
I defeated the Nergal.

1295
01:17:29,186 --> 01:17:31,355
Why are we still inside the Pillar?

1296
01:17:32,397 --> 01:17:37,027
{\an8}We're still here because
the King of Ash is still alive.

1297
01:17:37,110 --> 01:17:39,488
[gasping]

1298
01:17:42,532 --> 01:17:43,950
[water bubbling]

1299
01:17:44,034 --> 01:17:45,827
[calm music playing]

1300
01:17:57,631 --> 01:17:59,633
[electrical buzzing]

1301
01:18:01,635 --> 01:18:03,220
[pensive music playing]

1302
01:18:07,808 --> 01:18:09,976
[people murmuring]

1303
01:18:17,943 --> 01:18:21,363
[Pine's father] We should at least try and
get Pine evacuated to the upper levels.

1304
01:18:21,446 --> 01:18:23,240
I'll see if my connection can help.

1305
01:18:23,323 --> 01:18:25,701
[Pine's mother]
I pray our child can be spared.

1306
01:18:25,784 --> 01:18:27,953
Oh, Lord Mitra!

1307
01:18:28,036 --> 01:18:29,121
Please help us.

1308
01:18:31,289 --> 01:18:32,624
[Pine] <i>This world…</i>

1309
01:18:32,708 --> 01:18:33,917
<i>it's the worst.</i>

1310
01:18:35,460 --> 01:18:38,880
<i>But I think I'm the worst part about it.</i>

1311
01:18:39,881 --> 01:18:41,466
<i>Sapphire risked her life.</i>

1312
01:18:41,550 --> 01:18:43,343
<i>She fought to protect everyone.</i>

1313
01:18:43,927 --> 01:18:45,554
<i>What did I do?</i>

1314
01:18:45,637 --> 01:18:47,556
<i>Nothing at all.</i>

1315
01:18:49,599 --> 01:18:52,185
[Sapphire] Let's try and find something
we can do together.

1316
01:18:52,269 --> 01:18:55,981
But if that's the case,
then you're gonna have to be my friend.

1317
01:18:56,064 --> 01:18:57,107
[Pine] <i>Sapphire…</i>

1318
01:18:58,859 --> 01:19:00,527
<i>I'm supposed to be her friend.</i>

1319
01:19:01,862 --> 01:19:04,614
<i>I should've gone with her</i>
<i>when she was taken away.</i>

1320
01:19:06,700 --> 01:19:09,536
<i>I should have shared more, asked more.</i>

1321
01:19:09,619 --> 01:19:10,954
[Nergal screeches]

1322
01:19:11,037 --> 01:19:14,082
<i>I should've called out to her</i>
<i>when she needed support.</i>

1323
01:19:14,166 --> 01:19:15,208
[panting]

1324
01:19:15,292 --> 01:19:18,295
<i>I just let her go in alone,</i>
<i>even when it seemed hopeless.</i>

1325
01:19:18,920 --> 01:19:20,672
<i>I did nothing to help her.</i>

1326
01:19:21,882 --> 01:19:24,468
<i>I'm just the one</i>
<i>who always needs protecting.</i>

1327
01:19:24,551 --> 01:19:27,095
<i>As a friend, I'm a total failure.</i>

1328
01:19:27,179 --> 01:19:29,473
[panting]

1329
01:19:33,018 --> 01:19:34,019
[liquid bubbling]

1330
01:19:39,733 --> 01:19:43,069
This must be what was amplifying
her inexplicable energy.

1331
01:19:44,738 --> 01:19:46,323
Have you prepared the altar?

1332
01:19:47,073 --> 01:19:49,576
[Mitra] It will be ready shortly,
Your Holiness.

1333
01:19:49,659 --> 01:19:50,786
Excellent.

1334
01:19:50,869 --> 01:19:52,829
Gather the children for the ritual,

1335
01:19:52,913 --> 01:19:56,124
and any Mitra volunteers
willing to sacrifice their life.

1336
01:19:56,208 --> 01:19:57,334
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

1337
01:19:58,084 --> 01:20:00,545
It doesn't have to be this way.

1338
01:20:00,629 --> 01:20:03,799
Why are you still going
to sacrifice the orphans?

1339
01:20:03,882 --> 01:20:06,426
Why can't we sacrifice Sapphire instead?

1340
01:20:06,510 --> 01:20:08,220
She should be our sacrifice.

1341
01:20:08,303 --> 01:20:10,722
You still don't understand.

1342
01:20:10,806 --> 01:20:13,600
That would only be violence
for violence's sake.

1343
01:20:13,683 --> 01:20:17,604
On the contrary, that impulse
would only worsen the situation.

1344
01:20:17,687 --> 01:20:19,272
{\an8}But why?

1345
01:20:19,898 --> 01:20:22,275
{\an8}It is not a curse but a creed,

1346
01:20:22,359 --> 01:20:24,820
{\an8}the Nergal are the repetition
of life and death,

1347
01:20:24,903 --> 01:20:27,197
{\an8}of creation and destruction.

1348
01:20:27,280 --> 01:20:30,450
{\an8}Our emotions and memories
are bound to them.

1349
01:20:30,534 --> 01:20:33,912
{\an8}We are trapped in an endless cycle
of chaos and struggle

1350
01:20:33,995 --> 01:20:36,706
{\an8}where mankind
will never defeat the Nergal.

1351
01:20:36,790 --> 01:20:38,166
[tools hammering]

1352
01:20:38,250 --> 01:20:41,294
<i>All that we have to soothe us</i>
<i>is our prayers.</i>

1353
01:20:42,504 --> 01:20:45,215
<i>Only through heartfelt mourning</i>
<i>can we find calm</i>

1354
01:20:45,298 --> 01:20:47,759
<i>in this riotously irrational world.</i>

1355
01:20:48,802 --> 01:20:51,721
<i>We offer up our devotion</i>
<i>to the countless souls</i>

1356
01:20:51,805 --> 01:20:54,599
<i>and memories residing within the Nergal.</i>

1357
01:20:54,683 --> 01:20:58,353
<i>And for that, profound sorrow</i>
<i>and compassion are required.</i>

1358
01:20:58,436 --> 01:21:00,689
<i>Carved from the depths of the heart.</i>

1359
01:21:01,439 --> 01:21:05,735
<i>The pure souls of the orphans</i>
<i>that our church has so lovingly raised,</i>

1360
01:21:06,361 --> 01:21:09,739
<i>they are the fuel</i>
<i>for that compassion and sorrow.</i>

1361
01:21:11,324 --> 01:21:16,788
We Mitra have no feelings for that girl,
so she will not serve our purpose.

1362
01:21:16,872 --> 01:21:19,708
This is not Silverland.

1363
01:21:20,500 --> 01:21:24,921
It is only through pain and suffering
that our prayers are delivered.

1364
01:21:25,005 --> 01:21:29,301
Prayer without pain
is purposeless and ineffective.

1365
01:21:29,384 --> 01:21:30,677
[breathing shakily]

1366
01:21:31,511 --> 01:21:35,098
Now we begin our sacred work.

1367
01:21:35,181 --> 01:21:36,850
We will try to mitigate the losses

1368
01:21:36,933 --> 01:21:41,146
by minimizing the sacrifices
as much as we possibly can.

1369
01:21:43,607 --> 01:21:45,191
The time has come.

1370
01:21:45,275 --> 01:21:47,068
He is here.

1371
01:21:47,152 --> 01:21:49,571
[ominous music playing]

1372
01:21:49,654 --> 01:21:51,781
[panting]

1373
01:21:53,033 --> 01:21:54,743
It took you long enough, Pine.

1374
01:21:56,786 --> 01:21:57,954
I'm here.

1375
01:21:58,038 --> 01:22:00,415
We're all here together.

1376
01:22:01,750 --> 01:22:03,376
It's about to start.

1377
01:22:10,884 --> 01:22:13,762
All systems are functioning normally.

1378
01:22:13,845 --> 01:22:15,972
[rumbling]

1379
01:22:27,901 --> 01:22:33,281
[thunderous footsteps]

1380
01:22:33,365 --> 01:22:35,158
What's that?

1381
01:22:35,241 --> 01:22:37,243
That is the King of Ash.

1382
01:22:37,327 --> 01:22:39,913
Begin the holy ritual.

1383
01:22:41,122 --> 01:22:43,833
<i>♪ King ♪</i>

1384
01:22:43,917 --> 01:22:48,338
♪ <i>O King </i>♪

1385
01:22:48,421 --> 01:22:51,883
<i>♪ Grant me ♪</i>

1386
01:22:51,967 --> 01:22:57,055
<i>♪ Your divine guidance ♪</i>

1387
01:22:57,138 --> 01:23:00,976
<i>♪ For I am ♪</i>

1388
01:23:01,059 --> 01:23:06,314
<i>♪ A blue soul ♪</i>

1389
01:23:07,148 --> 01:23:10,026
<i>♪ Your faithful ♪</i>

1390
01:23:10,110 --> 01:23:15,573
<i>♪ Angel of prayer ♪</i>

1391
01:23:25,500 --> 01:23:27,877
<i>♪ King ♪</i>

1392
01:23:27,961 --> 01:23:32,507
<i>♪ O King ♪</i>

1393
01:23:32,590 --> 01:23:35,969
<i>♪ Grant me ♪</i>

1394
01:23:36,052 --> 01:23:41,016
<i>♪ Pure joy ♪</i>

1395
01:23:41,099 --> 01:23:47,355
<i>♪ For I am</i>
<i>A blue destiny ♪</i>

1396
01:23:47,439 --> 01:23:51,109
And in the end,
I wasn't able to help anyone.

1397
01:23:52,110 --> 01:23:54,654
And even worse, it's my fault.

1398
01:23:55,947 --> 01:23:57,615
[Zirco] Unbelievable!

1399
01:23:58,658 --> 01:24:00,994
[gasps] Look over there.

1400
01:24:01,077 --> 01:24:02,579
-It's Sapphire!
-[all gasp]

1401
01:24:02,662 --> 01:24:04,330
[Zirco] It is Sapphire!

1402
01:24:04,414 --> 01:24:07,125
[Rock] But why isn't she transforming?

1403
01:24:07,208 --> 01:24:09,127
[groans softly]

1404
01:24:09,210 --> 01:24:11,546
[gasps] It's gone!

1405
01:24:12,547 --> 01:24:14,215
Where's her ribbon?

1406
01:24:14,299 --> 01:24:16,134
She can't use her power without it!

1407
01:24:16,885 --> 01:24:18,344
[Hecate] Where did it go?

1408
01:24:18,428 --> 01:24:21,347
[Tack and Chick exclaiming]

1409
01:24:24,267 --> 01:24:26,102
It's almost complete.

1410
01:24:26,186 --> 01:24:28,438
All that remains
is to offer up the orphans.

1411
01:24:29,606 --> 01:24:34,569
And with this, let our prayers be heard
and the King of Ash be pacified.

1412
01:24:34,652 --> 01:24:38,031
We cannot allow their lives to be wasted.

1413
01:24:38,114 --> 01:24:40,033
[breathing shakily]

1414
01:24:41,326 --> 01:24:43,953
<i>♪ King ♪</i>

1415
01:24:44,037 --> 01:24:47,916
<i>♪ O King ♪</i>

1416
01:24:48,833 --> 01:24:53,338
<i>♪ Grant me</i>
<i>Your warm embrace ♪</i>

1417
01:24:53,421 --> 01:24:55,256
[yelling]

1418
01:24:56,132 --> 01:24:57,258
Stop right there!

1419
01:24:57,342 --> 01:24:59,677
[singing continues] <i>♪ For I am ♪</i>

1420
01:24:59,761 --> 01:25:03,014
<i>♪ A blue bud ♪</i>

1421
01:25:05,642 --> 01:25:06,935
Velvet, wait!

1422
01:25:07,852 --> 01:25:09,479
[Mitra guard] Don't let him get away!

1423
01:25:09,562 --> 01:25:10,730
[screeching]

1424
01:25:10,814 --> 01:25:12,482
What's the commotion?

1425
01:25:12,565 --> 01:25:15,235
Your Holiness,
it appears Velvet has escaped.

1426
01:25:15,318 --> 01:25:17,695
-Capture him at once.
-Yes, sir.

1427
01:25:17,779 --> 01:25:19,322
[effort scream]

1428
01:25:20,907 --> 01:25:22,826
-[grunting]
-[swords clashing]

1429
01:25:25,328 --> 01:25:27,080
What are those immigrants doing here?

1430
01:25:27,163 --> 01:25:28,998
[Mitra guard]
Don't let them get any closer!

1431
01:25:29,082 --> 01:25:30,041
Huh?

1432
01:25:32,001 --> 01:25:33,044
[exclaims]

1433
01:25:33,128 --> 01:25:34,504
[whimpering]

1434
01:25:35,839 --> 01:25:37,132
Give that back!

1435
01:25:37,799 --> 01:25:38,758
[guard grunts]

1436
01:25:38,842 --> 01:25:40,552
[Pope] Stop him! He mustn't get away!

1437
01:25:41,469 --> 01:25:42,387
Chick!

1438
01:25:43,054 --> 01:25:45,557
-Got it!
-We're counting on you!

1439
01:25:45,640 --> 01:25:46,599
[exclaims]

1440
01:25:46,683 --> 01:25:47,934
[guards grunting]

1441
01:25:49,394 --> 01:25:50,478
[guard] Get over here!

1442
01:25:50,562 --> 01:25:52,105
-Hecate!
-Leave it to me!

1443
01:25:52,730 --> 01:25:54,691
[all grunting]

1444
01:25:54,774 --> 01:25:56,192
[effort scream]

1445
01:25:56,276 --> 01:25:57,443
[straining]

1446
01:25:59,779 --> 01:26:00,989
Hecate, over here!

1447
01:26:01,739 --> 01:26:03,116
-[grunts]
-Whoa!

1448
01:26:03,199 --> 01:26:04,492
Pine!

1449
01:26:04,576 --> 01:26:05,743
Grab on!

1450
01:26:05,827 --> 01:26:07,036
[gasping]

1451
01:26:07,662 --> 01:26:08,788
[effort scream]

1452
01:26:09,998 --> 01:26:11,040
[straining]

1453
01:26:12,208 --> 01:26:14,085
[yelling]

1454
01:26:15,712 --> 01:26:17,297
[Rock grunting]

1455
01:26:19,340 --> 01:26:20,383
[grunting]

1456
01:26:21,009 --> 01:26:22,177
{\an8}Pine!

1457
01:26:22,260 --> 01:26:23,553
{\an8}Go!

1458
01:26:24,804 --> 01:26:26,514
Sapphire!

1459
01:26:38,359 --> 01:26:40,987
I know I don't have the power
to save the world,

1460
01:26:41,070 --> 01:26:43,656
but I couldn't just
sit back and do nothing.

1461
01:26:43,740 --> 01:26:47,452
You're always there to protect me,
but I needed to do something for myself.

1462
01:26:48,620 --> 01:26:50,205
[Sapphire] Thanks, Pine.

1463
01:26:50,288 --> 01:26:54,292
But maybe this wasn't
the reason why I survived.

1464
01:26:55,126 --> 01:26:57,378
{\an8}The reason why you survived?

1465
01:26:57,462 --> 01:26:59,923
{\an8}The only reason I need
is that you're my best friend.

1466
01:27:00,006 --> 01:27:00,965
{\an8}You're Sapphire.

1467
01:27:01,049 --> 01:27:02,008
[gasps]

1468
01:27:02,717 --> 01:27:04,761
But I'm so weak.

1469
01:27:05,386 --> 01:27:06,930
I don't think I can win.

1470
01:27:07,680 --> 01:27:08,765
I'm just…

1471
01:27:08,848 --> 01:27:09,933
I'm cursed.

1472
01:27:13,394 --> 01:27:16,898
{\an8}A curse is something that's made of words.

1473
01:27:16,981 --> 01:27:19,567
And that means words can break them.

1474
01:27:20,235 --> 01:27:21,319
[Sapphire] Huh?

1475
01:27:21,402 --> 01:27:24,072
Sapphire, you've been
fighting for so long.

1476
01:27:25,406 --> 01:27:27,575
It's just been one big struggle.

1477
01:27:27,659 --> 01:27:29,035
[gasps softly]

1478
01:27:29,118 --> 01:27:31,788
You've been through so much suffering.

1479
01:27:31,871 --> 01:27:34,290
{\an8}But you've made it this far, haven't you?

1480
01:27:34,374 --> 01:27:36,542
{\an8}How can you say you're weak?

1481
01:27:36,626 --> 01:27:38,544
{\an8}You're the Princess Knight,

1482
01:27:38,628 --> 01:27:41,756
and that makes you my hero!

1483
01:27:42,507 --> 01:27:43,758
[Sapphire sighs]

1484
01:27:47,762 --> 01:27:48,972
[Sapphire breathing shakily]

1485
01:27:50,932 --> 01:27:52,517
Thank you, Pine.

1486
01:27:52,600 --> 01:27:54,185
I needed that.

1487
01:27:54,269 --> 01:27:57,146
[screeching]

1488
01:28:00,692 --> 01:28:02,318
[yelling]

1489
01:28:03,861 --> 01:28:05,822
[Mitra guard] No, you don't.

1490
01:28:07,073 --> 01:28:09,117
[yelling]

1491
01:28:10,702 --> 01:28:13,371
Nazuna, Hakobe! Don't worry.

1492
01:28:14,080 --> 01:28:15,456
I've got you now.

1493
01:28:17,292 --> 01:28:19,043
-Is that you, Velvet?
-Is that you, Velvet?

1494
01:28:20,878 --> 01:28:22,922
Is this is really where it all ends?

1495
01:28:23,506 --> 01:28:24,882
Someone, please!

1496
01:28:36,311 --> 01:28:37,895
[grunting]

1497
01:28:39,230 --> 01:28:41,858
The Princess Knight, to the rescue!

1498
01:28:44,694 --> 01:28:47,155
-The Princess Knight…
-To the rescue!

1499
01:28:48,031 --> 01:28:50,116
Sapphire, how did you…

1500
01:28:53,786 --> 01:28:56,080
Don't worry, guys, let me handle this.

1501
01:28:56,748 --> 01:28:58,541
Try and get everyone to safety.

1502
01:28:58,624 --> 01:29:00,752
Can you really save them?

1503
01:29:00,835 --> 01:29:02,879
And I don't just mean the children,

1504
01:29:02,962 --> 01:29:04,756
but the people in the country, too.

1505
01:29:05,381 --> 01:29:06,549
Watch me.

1506
01:29:07,300 --> 01:29:09,552
It's what I'm meant to do with this power.

1507
01:29:10,887 --> 01:29:12,055
[gasps softly]

1508
01:29:13,306 --> 01:29:14,349
[giggles]

1509
01:29:14,891 --> 01:29:16,601
[captivating music playing]

1510
01:29:21,939 --> 01:29:23,524
[roaring]

1511
01:29:28,237 --> 01:29:30,198
[electrical buzzing]

1512
01:29:31,866 --> 01:29:36,245
{\an8}7 YEARS EARLIER

1513
01:29:38,206 --> 01:29:42,168
[calm music playing]

1514
01:29:44,212 --> 01:29:46,047
[child giggles]

1515
01:29:49,008 --> 01:29:50,009
[both gasp]

1516
01:29:54,680 --> 01:29:55,890
[gasps]

1517
01:30:01,312 --> 01:30:03,231
[grunting softly]

1518
01:30:03,314 --> 01:30:04,732
Where am I?

1519
01:30:04,816 --> 01:30:05,817
Wait, I remember you.

1520
01:30:07,693 --> 01:30:09,028
Huh? [grunts]

1521
01:30:11,405 --> 01:30:12,490
Huh.

1522
01:30:17,120 --> 01:30:18,246
Is anyone there?

1523
01:30:18,329 --> 01:30:20,081
[echoing]

1524
01:30:35,888 --> 01:30:37,807
-[doors thud]
-[Sapphire grunting]

1525
01:30:37,890 --> 01:30:40,685
[orchestral music playing]

1526
01:30:40,768 --> 01:30:42,019
[gasps]

1527
01:30:42,770 --> 01:30:44,772
Is there anyone here?

1528
01:30:46,607 --> 01:30:47,900
[man] You've done well.

1529
01:30:47,984 --> 01:30:49,193
[Sapphire gasps]

1530
01:30:49,861 --> 01:30:51,320
Who are you?

1531
01:30:52,113 --> 01:30:54,031
{\an8}It looks like you don't remember.

1532
01:30:55,616 --> 01:30:57,243
Uh…

1533
01:30:57,326 --> 01:30:58,995
Don't be afraid.

1534
01:30:59,078 --> 01:31:01,998
Here no one can be hurt anymore.

1535
01:31:02,081 --> 01:31:03,249
[Sapphire] What do you mean?

1536
01:31:03,332 --> 01:31:07,170
It means you carried out your role
and fulfilled your destiny.

1537
01:31:07,795 --> 01:31:08,796
[Sapphire] Chorogy?

1538
01:31:08,880 --> 01:31:10,089
Is that really you?

1539
01:31:10,173 --> 01:31:11,132
Of course.

1540
01:31:11,215 --> 01:31:12,508
[gasps]

1541
01:31:13,801 --> 01:31:14,844
[Sapphire] Thank goodness!

1542
01:31:14,927 --> 01:31:17,597
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry I couldn't save you.

1543
01:31:17,680 --> 01:31:19,015
Forgive me! [sobs]

1544
01:31:19,974 --> 01:31:20,892
But who's he?

1545
01:31:20,975 --> 01:31:24,562
One of the many other heroes
who challenged the Nergal.

1546
01:31:24,645 --> 01:31:26,314
So he's just like us, I guess.

1547
01:31:26,898 --> 01:31:28,191
You fought them, too?

1548
01:31:28,274 --> 01:31:29,317
You fought the Nergal?

1549
01:31:29,901 --> 01:31:33,196
{\an8}I did. But now that painful battle
is at an end.

1550
01:31:34,488 --> 01:31:35,573
It's as I said,

1551
01:31:35,656 --> 01:31:38,034
in this place,
no one hurts, no one suffers.

1552
01:31:38,743 --> 01:31:42,038
A place within history and memory
where all who reside,

1553
01:31:42,121 --> 01:31:43,873
live in peace and contentment.

1554
01:31:45,041 --> 01:31:48,002
An alternate reality,
something that could have been.

1555
01:31:49,128 --> 01:31:51,088
It is an endless story.

1556
01:31:52,256 --> 01:31:55,134
Ash is the soul scorched by the flame.

1557
01:31:56,177 --> 01:31:57,762
It is death itself,

1558
01:31:58,721 --> 01:32:00,973
and in death, each soul is purified.

1559
01:32:01,057 --> 01:32:02,308
And in time, is reborn.

1560
01:32:03,643 --> 01:32:06,187
This is a place
where those souls can rest.

1561
01:32:07,313 --> 01:32:08,814
[gasps]

1562
01:32:09,815 --> 01:32:12,151
It's the kind of fate people long for.

1563
01:32:12,235 --> 01:32:14,153
[Sapphire] No, this is a dream.

1564
01:32:14,237 --> 01:32:16,656
Everyone outside hasn't given up.

1565
01:32:16,739 --> 01:32:18,824
So makes what you think I will?

1566
01:32:18,908 --> 01:32:20,159
[scoffs]

1567
01:32:20,243 --> 01:32:22,453
Someone's been awaiting your arrival.

1568
01:32:23,913 --> 01:32:25,623
[rumbling]

1569
01:32:26,791 --> 01:32:27,792
{\an8}BEFORE THE ALTAR

1570
01:32:27,875 --> 01:32:29,669
{\an8}[Pope grunts]

1571
01:32:31,128 --> 01:32:32,922
What has that girl done?

1572
01:32:33,547 --> 01:32:36,050
It hasn't moved since she toppled it.

1573
01:32:36,133 --> 01:32:37,885
Is she all right in there?

1574
01:32:39,345 --> 01:32:40,846
Sapphire, you…

1575
01:32:40,930 --> 01:32:42,556
[machinery clanking]

1576
01:32:42,640 --> 01:32:44,517
Time to put this to use.

1577
01:32:44,600 --> 01:32:46,060
INSIDE THE NERGAL

1578
01:32:46,143 --> 01:32:48,271
-[gentle music playing]
-[people chattering]

1579
01:32:49,563 --> 01:32:50,731
[Sapphire] And then…

1580
01:32:50,815 --> 01:32:53,693
Then I took down the Nergal
like it was nothing.

1581
01:32:53,776 --> 01:32:54,944
What do you think?

1582
01:32:55,027 --> 01:32:56,070
Pretty amazing, right?

1583
01:32:56,153 --> 01:32:59,198
[Queen] Yes, darling.
You are quite amazing, Sapphire.

1584
01:32:59,282 --> 01:33:00,825
[giggling]

1585
01:33:00,908 --> 01:33:02,034
You know…

1586
01:33:02,118 --> 01:33:06,372
Mama, since I was a little girl,
all I ever wanted was to hear your praise.

1587
01:33:06,455 --> 01:33:08,207
Oh, Sapphire.

1588
01:33:08,291 --> 01:33:09,417
[Sapphire] I was a handful.

1589
01:33:09,500 --> 01:33:12,211
You were always getting mad at me
for something.

1590
01:33:12,295 --> 01:33:15,423
But all I ever wanted to hear
was, "Good job," or, "That's my girl."

1591
01:33:15,506 --> 01:33:16,716
You know?

1592
01:33:16,799 --> 01:33:17,883
That's all.

1593
01:33:17,967 --> 01:33:20,678
Sapphire, you never did anything wrong.

1594
01:33:20,761 --> 01:33:23,097
I couldn't bear the thought of losing you.

1595
01:33:23,180 --> 01:33:25,516
You meant more than the world to me

1596
01:33:25,599 --> 01:33:27,852
and I made you suffer for it.

1597
01:33:29,145 --> 01:33:31,814
Don't say that, Mother. It's fine.

1598
01:33:31,897 --> 01:33:34,275
{\an8}Let's start over from the beginning.

1599
01:33:34,859 --> 01:33:36,235
I want to apologize.

1600
01:33:36,319 --> 01:33:38,195
Darling, I'm sorry.

1601
01:33:38,279 --> 01:33:40,823
I thought I was
protecting you in the past.

1602
01:33:40,906 --> 01:33:42,825
I was obsessed with your training.

1603
01:33:42,908 --> 01:33:45,077
It was arrogance, nothing more.

1604
01:33:45,161 --> 01:33:46,871
And it ended up hurting you.

1605
01:33:48,122 --> 01:33:49,749
Only now can I say it.

1606
01:33:49,832 --> 01:33:52,293
{\an8}My words must have cut like a sword.

1607
01:33:52,376 --> 01:33:54,879
My silence must have
bound you like chains.

1608
01:33:54,962 --> 01:33:57,631
[sobs] Never did I imagine
I would experience

1609
01:33:57,715 --> 01:33:59,300
such deep regret as a mother.

1610
01:34:00,468 --> 01:34:01,719
Oh, Mother!

1611
01:34:03,220 --> 01:34:04,680
[chiming]

1612
01:34:04,764 --> 01:34:08,768
[Pine and Velvet]
Don't give in! Come back to reality!

1613
01:34:08,851 --> 01:34:12,313
<i>♪ Long, long ago ♪</i>

1614
01:34:12,396 --> 01:34:15,358
<i>♪ A lone girl ♪</i>

1615
01:34:15,441 --> 01:34:18,444
<i>♪ Wandered the land ♪</i>

1616
01:34:18,527 --> 01:34:20,279
[Sembry]
Do you think this'll actually work?

1617
01:34:20,363 --> 01:34:21,822
It will!

1618
01:34:21,906 --> 01:34:25,076
-Don't give up! Sapphire!
-Sapphire, we believe in you!

1619
01:34:25,159 --> 01:34:26,243
[gasps]

1620
01:34:26,327 --> 01:34:28,412
[Queen] What's the matter, Sapphire?

1621
01:34:28,496 --> 01:34:31,499
<i>♪ The poor villagers… ♪</i>

1622
01:34:31,582 --> 01:34:33,876
Mother, Father…

1623
01:34:33,959 --> 01:34:37,004
[Queen] You still can't forgive me,
can you, my darling?

1624
01:34:37,755 --> 01:34:39,590
I suppose I understand.

1625
01:34:39,673 --> 01:34:42,843
But I just wanted to see
your beautiful face once more.

1626
01:34:43,636 --> 01:34:46,722
[Sapphire] Oh, Mother,
I wanted to see your face, too.

1627
01:34:46,806 --> 01:34:48,849
I want to throw this door open.

1628
01:34:48,933 --> 01:34:51,811
I want to live with everyone
here in Silverland again.

1629
01:34:51,894 --> 01:34:53,312
But this…

1630
01:34:53,938 --> 01:34:55,398
This place…

1631
01:34:55,481 --> 01:34:56,899
it isn't real.

1632
01:34:58,776 --> 01:34:59,902
[crying]

1633
01:34:59,985 --> 01:35:01,445
[Queen] <i>Here's a present for you.</i>

1634
01:35:01,529 --> 01:35:03,406
[King] <i>It looks wonderful on her!</i>

1635
01:35:03,489 --> 01:35:06,325
-[Queen] <i>I love you, Sapphire.</i>
-[King] <i>I love you so much!</i>

1636
01:35:06,409 --> 01:35:07,868
[sobs]

1637
01:35:07,952 --> 01:35:14,083
{\an8}♪ <i>You offered the same prayer</i>
<i>Again and again </i>♪

1638
01:35:15,751 --> 01:35:18,170
{\an8}[Sapphire] I'm thankful you finally
made me realize it.

1639
01:35:19,255 --> 01:35:21,757
{\an8}[sobbing] For the first time ever,
I can say it.

1640
01:35:21,841 --> 01:35:25,010
{\an8}Both Mother and Father are dead.

1641
01:35:25,094 --> 01:35:27,555
{\an8}I'm heartbroken. It hurts.

1642
01:35:30,891 --> 01:35:32,560
[sniffling]

1643
01:35:34,770 --> 01:35:36,981
[footsteps approaching]

1644
01:35:42,778 --> 01:35:44,447
[whooshing]

1645
01:35:50,327 --> 01:35:52,204
The factor of the King of Ash.

1646
01:35:52,288 --> 01:35:53,497
There it is.

1647
01:35:54,248 --> 01:35:55,916
So…

1648
01:35:56,000 --> 01:36:00,296
you've chosen the pain of reality
over the peace of memories?

1649
01:36:00,963 --> 01:36:02,256
That's right.

1650
01:36:02,882 --> 01:36:04,383
[chiming]

1651
01:36:05,759 --> 01:36:08,387
'Cause I'm… the Princess Knight.

1652
01:36:18,939 --> 01:36:19,982
Attack!

1653
01:36:21,108 --> 01:36:22,860
[Sapphire grunting]

1654
01:36:22,943 --> 01:36:24,236
[grunting]

1655
01:36:25,779 --> 01:36:26,906
[Sapphire straining]

1656
01:36:32,161 --> 01:36:32,995
[grunting]

1657
01:36:33,829 --> 01:36:35,289
[Velvet] Sapphire! Get down!

1658
01:36:38,459 --> 01:36:39,376
Amazing!

1659
01:36:40,794 --> 01:36:42,004
Thanks for that!

1660
01:36:42,087 --> 01:36:43,047
Get to the Factor.

1661
01:36:43,130 --> 01:36:44,381
Leave them to us.

1662
01:36:47,384 --> 01:36:48,928
[grunts]

1663
01:36:51,096 --> 01:36:52,598
Sapphire!

1664
01:36:52,681 --> 01:36:55,226
[effort scream]

1665
01:36:56,018 --> 01:36:57,853
[grunting]

1666
01:36:57,937 --> 01:36:59,146
Why you…

1667
01:36:59,230 --> 01:37:01,148
[Sapphire yelling]

1668
01:37:02,274 --> 01:37:03,734
What's happening now?

1669
01:37:03,817 --> 01:37:05,027
[grunts]

1670
01:37:05,110 --> 01:37:07,071
[Sapphire exclaiming, yelling]

1671
01:37:07,780 --> 01:37:09,406
[screaming]

1672
01:37:15,704 --> 01:37:16,830
I'm not done yet!

1673
01:37:16,914 --> 01:37:18,624
[straining]

1674
01:37:19,291 --> 01:37:21,669
[panting]

1675
01:37:22,253 --> 01:37:24,505
There's nothing you can do, Sapphire.

1676
01:37:24,588 --> 01:37:26,173
[Sapphire grunting]

1677
01:37:30,219 --> 01:37:31,887
And it's not just you.

1678
01:37:31,971 --> 01:37:33,639
No one in here can stop it.

1679
01:37:33,722 --> 01:37:36,892
Well then, I'm glad there are
people outside fighting.

1680
01:37:37,560 --> 01:37:39,603
[both grunting]

1681
01:37:40,938 --> 01:37:42,398
[Sapphire] I can't fail.

1682
01:37:42,481 --> 01:37:44,900
This time, I have to protect everyone,

1683
01:37:45,484 --> 01:37:47,319
or I'll never be saved!

1684
01:37:49,280 --> 01:37:50,364
-Sorry. [grunts]
-[groans]

1685
01:37:50,447 --> 01:37:52,741
But my peace and fulfillment

1686
01:37:53,284 --> 01:37:54,660
aren't found here!

1687
01:37:56,996 --> 01:37:58,956
You'll never win!

1688
01:37:59,790 --> 01:38:02,334
[straining]

1689
01:38:02,418 --> 01:38:03,877
[Sapphire grunts]

1690
01:38:05,379 --> 01:38:07,172
[Sapphire] Ow, that hurt.

1691
01:38:07,256 --> 01:38:09,216
I'll make you pay for that.

1692
01:38:09,300 --> 01:38:10,342
Huh? They're gone!

1693
01:38:10,426 --> 01:38:11,719
[scoffs]

1694
01:38:12,261 --> 01:38:15,306
This has happened countless times before.

1695
01:38:15,389 --> 01:38:17,725
And not a single hero
has changed the cycle.

1696
01:38:19,018 --> 01:38:20,144
Oh, yeah?

1697
01:38:20,811 --> 01:38:24,898
[grunts] Take that, and that, and that,
and that, and that, and that, and that,

1698
01:38:24,982 --> 01:38:28,235
and that, and that, and that, and that,
and that, and that, and that…

1699
01:38:28,319 --> 01:38:30,362
Huh? [screams]

1700
01:38:35,701 --> 01:38:37,244
Go on. It's yours.

1701
01:38:37,328 --> 01:38:38,829
[Sapphire exclaims]

1702
01:38:38,912 --> 01:38:40,122
[yelling]

1703
01:38:40,205 --> 01:38:41,749
[clatters]

1704
01:38:45,169 --> 01:38:47,212
It's impossible, Sapphire. Forget it.

1705
01:38:47,296 --> 01:38:49,632
Get out of the way!

1706
01:38:52,384 --> 01:38:53,802
[both] Sapphire!

1707
01:38:56,388 --> 01:38:58,390
[Sapphire grunting]

1708
01:38:58,474 --> 01:39:00,643
Yoo-hoo!

1709
01:39:00,726 --> 01:39:02,061
Catch me now, Donkey!

1710
01:39:02,144 --> 01:39:04,980
[both] Do it, Sapphire!

1711
01:39:05,064 --> 01:39:06,940
[growling in frustration]

1712
01:39:07,024 --> 01:39:08,734
[Sapphire grunts]

1713
01:39:16,867 --> 01:39:18,869
[all straining]

1714
01:39:22,206 --> 01:39:26,251
[all yelling]

1715
01:39:40,224 --> 01:39:45,104
[screaming] You can't change this world!

1716
01:39:45,187 --> 01:39:46,980
[Sapphire grunting]

1717
01:39:47,606 --> 01:39:51,360
Even if I can't, I'm still gonna try.

1718
01:39:53,112 --> 01:39:54,113
All right.

1719
01:40:01,286 --> 01:40:02,996
[effort scream]

1720
01:40:06,333 --> 01:40:08,210
[screeching]

1721
01:40:13,590 --> 01:40:15,342
[all gasping]

1722
01:40:15,426 --> 01:40:17,261
[straining]

1723
01:40:18,262 --> 01:40:19,888
[bubbling]

1724
01:40:19,972 --> 01:40:21,849
[screaming]

1725
01:40:24,309 --> 01:40:25,686
[dramatic music]

1726
01:40:30,899 --> 01:40:32,443
[applause]

1727
01:40:33,235 --> 01:40:35,195
[people cheering]

1728
01:40:37,364 --> 01:40:39,158
[gentle music playing]

1729
01:40:40,617 --> 01:40:41,702
TAKARAZUKA REVUE

1730
01:40:43,328 --> 01:40:46,457
[crowd] Encore! Encore!

1731
01:40:46,540 --> 01:40:50,794
Encore! Encore! Encore!

1732
01:40:50,878 --> 01:40:53,422
Were you destined to be me somewhere else?

1733
01:40:53,505 --> 01:40:55,716
Are you another version of my soul?

1734
01:40:57,134 --> 01:40:59,052
Thank you for everything.

1735
01:41:00,220 --> 01:41:04,850
I hope the new world that you're going to
is a beautiful and happy one.

1736
01:41:04,933 --> 01:41:06,977
[music continues]

1737
01:41:09,062 --> 01:41:11,440
PRINCESS KNIGHT
OSAMU TEZUKA

1738
01:41:16,528 --> 01:41:17,946
[screeching]

1739
01:41:21,200 --> 01:41:24,161
[Sapphire]
<i>May all these souls at last find peace.</i>

1740
01:41:24,244 --> 01:41:25,829
[triumphant music playing]

1741
01:41:38,217 --> 01:41:40,385
[people exclaiming]

1742
01:41:43,639 --> 01:41:45,891
[music continues]

1743
01:41:49,603 --> 01:41:51,438
[all gasping]

1744
01:41:51,522 --> 01:41:53,398
Sapphire, you did it!

1745
01:41:53,482 --> 01:41:55,359
She saved us!

1746
01:41:56,276 --> 01:41:57,820
[chuckles softly]

1747
01:42:01,240 --> 01:42:02,741
[Sapphire panting]

1748
01:42:02,825 --> 01:42:04,576
[Sapphire] Hey, guys!

1749
01:42:04,660 --> 01:42:06,078
-Huh?
-[Sapphire] Hey, you guys!

1750
01:42:06,912 --> 01:42:08,831
[Pine laughs]

1751
01:42:08,914 --> 01:42:11,166
-[Zirco] Sapphire!
-[all] You did it! Sapphire!

1752
01:42:11,250 --> 01:42:12,501
[Sapphire laughing]

1753
01:42:13,752 --> 01:42:15,546
Why do you all look like
you've seen a ghost?

1754
01:42:15,629 --> 01:42:17,005
Did you ever doubt me?

1755
01:42:18,090 --> 01:42:21,718
The Princess Knight to the rescue again!

1756
01:42:23,136 --> 01:42:27,641
I would have let the world burn
if it meant I'd be saving these children.

1757
01:42:27,724 --> 01:42:30,435
And I imagine that's how
your parents felt, too.

1758
01:42:32,479 --> 01:42:33,897
You might be right.

1759
01:42:35,190 --> 01:42:37,609
What will the Princess Knight do now?

1760
01:42:37,693 --> 01:42:40,612
I'd be happy to help
in any way that I can.

1761
01:42:41,405 --> 01:42:46,535
Thanks, but first, I'm going
to pay a visit to Silver Land.

1762
01:42:46,618 --> 01:42:49,121
I have to pay my respects.

1763
01:42:49,204 --> 01:42:52,082
Mourn Mother, Father and the kingdom.

1764
01:42:53,584 --> 01:42:55,544
You can bet I'm coming, too!

1765
01:42:55,627 --> 01:42:56,628
[Sapphire chuckles]

1766
01:42:56,712 --> 01:42:59,256
[all] What?!

1767
01:42:59,339 --> 01:43:00,924
Come on!

1768
01:43:01,008 --> 01:43:02,801
Don't make this any harder.

1769
01:43:05,596 --> 01:43:08,265
So you're really leaving us?

1770
01:43:08,348 --> 01:43:10,225
I've made up my mind.

1771
01:43:10,309 --> 01:43:12,477
But once I get there,
I'll write to you, Pine.

1772
01:43:12,561 --> 01:43:15,314
If you and the others
hadn't been there cheering me on,

1773
01:43:15,397 --> 01:43:17,065
I never would have won.

1774
01:43:17,774 --> 01:43:20,277
Because Pine, you were
the one who broke my curse.

1775
01:43:20,819 --> 01:43:22,362
[giggles]

1776
01:43:22,446 --> 01:43:23,614
Sapphire!

1777
01:43:23,697 --> 01:43:25,657
[Sapphire grunts, chuckles]

1778
01:43:25,741 --> 01:43:29,244
I'll visit.
I'll come and see you in Silver Land.

1779
01:43:29,328 --> 01:43:31,997
'Cause, we're friends.
Friends forever, right?

1780
01:43:32,831 --> 01:43:35,000
Yeah, we're all friends forever.

1781
01:43:36,543 --> 01:43:38,962
[triumphant music playing]

1782
01:43:39,046 --> 01:43:42,466
[Sapphire] <i>Not a single Nergal</i>
<i>appeared again since then.</i>

1783
01:43:42,549 --> 01:43:45,802
<i>It seemed like at long last,</i>
<i>the cycle had been broken.</i>

1784
01:43:46,678 --> 01:43:51,600
<i>I hope someday,</i>
<i>or better yet, starting now,</i>

1785
01:43:51,683 --> 01:43:54,686
<i>I hope that the people</i>
<i>who have been hurt can begin to heal,</i>

1786
01:43:54,770 --> 01:43:56,605
<i>however slowly.</i>

1787
01:43:56,688 --> 01:44:00,025
<i>And that their newfound future</i>
<i>is brilliantly bright.</i>

1788
01:44:02,945 --> 01:44:04,947
[closing theme music playing]

1789
01:46:52,989 --> 01:46:54,991
["The Winter-Worn Traveler" playing]